(window.PF_CAT_SHARD=window.PF_CAT_SHARD||{})["76454"]={"1767":{"i":"1767","entryRequirements":"a)\tCandidates are required to have gained:\n\r\ni.\tan undergraduate degree assessed as relevant by the Team Manager, or\n\r\nii.\ta qualification approved as equivalent by the Team Manager.\n\n\n\r\nb)\tCandidates who have not gained a relevant undergraduate degree or equivalent qualification may submit a portfolio and, if the application is successful, may be admitted on an ad eundum statem basis.\n\n\n\r\nc)\tCandidates for the Postgraduate Diploma in Health and Social Practice, (Professional Supervision), and the Postgraduate Certificates in Professional Supervision are required to have a minimum of two years post qualifying experience in their professional field of practice or the equivalent.).  This is in recognition of the requirement to have consolidated and developed their own practice to a level sufficient to embark in the role of supervisor of others.\n\r\nd)\tCandidates for the Postgraduate Diploma in Health and Social Practice (Midwifery) and the Postgraduate Certificate in Midwifery are required to:\n\r\ni.\tbe registered with the Midwifery Council of New Zealand; and\n\r\nii.\thold a current Annual Practising Certificate; and \n\r\niii.\thave a minimum of one-year post-qualifying experience in midwifery practice (or the equivalent as approved by the selection committee).   \n\r\niv.\tand be in practice for an average minimum of 16 hours per week over a year.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Diploma in Health and Social Practice, with optional endorsements in Professional Supervision, Midwifery, and Mental Health and Addiction, will have developed advanced knowledge and skills for practice and career progression.  An interdisciplinary context will enable graduates to extend their capacity for critical and professional/clinical reasoning for specialist practice, leadership, management and supervision in complex professional environments.  The programme will be relevant to practitioners from a wide range of professional contexts.  Graduates will have developed a range of flexible skills and expertise which will position them well to be responsive to changing social service and health communities.  Learning and participating within the interdisciplinary teaching/learning context will enable graduates to transfer this experience to workplace relationships and networks.\n\n\n\r\nThe programme has four embedded qualifications: the Postgraduate Certificate in Health and Social Practice, the Postgraduate Certificate in Processional supervision, the Postgraduate Certificate in Midwifery, and the Postgraduate Certificate in Mental Health and Addiction.\n\n\n\r\nThe Postgraduate Diploma in Health and Social Practice will position graduates well to move into Masters level qualifications at other New Zealand universities and ITP's.\n\n\n\r\nGraduates will also have gained advanced knowledge and skills for practice and career progression within their field of practice and for leadership and management roles within the health and social service sector. The Professional Supervision endorsement graduates are well equipped for supervision roles in both health and social services in independent and specialised practice.The Midwifery endorsement graduates will have specialised midwifery knowledge which can lead to higher level professional development. The Mental Health and Addiction endorsement graduates will have specialised and applied mental health and addiction knowledge with which to gain entry into the mental health and addiction industry.","graduateProfile":"A graduate of the Postgraduate Diploma in Health and Social Practice will:\n\r\n*\tArticulate a critical, contextualised analysis of a relevant health and social service practice and its advancement \n\r\n*\tDemonstrate analytic rigour in evaluating  knowledge for expert practice within interdisciplinary environments\n\r\n*\tProvide effective health and social service leadership, supervisory, management and consultancy within interdisciplinary contexts\n\r\n*\tArticulate a professional body of knowledge and its relationship to ethical codes of practice\n\r\n*\tRespond to the demands and challenges of professional practice using reflexive strategies to nurture and cultivate the professional self\n\r\n*\tInfluence health and social practice and/or policies at organisational, regional and national levels\n\r\n*\tUse critical enquiry approaches to evaluate research findings for health and social service practice \n\r\n*\tImplement  highly effective communication and advocacy strategies with colleagues and clients in cultural, organisational, and professional contexts\n\r\n*\tCritically analyse and address issues of power and authority in relationship with clients, colleagues and organisations","educationPathway":"The Postgraduate Diploma in Health and Social Practice will position graduates well to move into Master's level qualifications at other New Zealand universities and ITP's.","developedBy":"Waikato Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=1767"},"1768":{"i":"1768","entryRequirements":"Undergraduate degree in Health and Social Practice or related discipline, or presentation of a portfolio of evidence to demonstrate best practice in Health and/or Social Practice or related professional context, including the ability to analyse and generate solutions to complex situations.  A Portfolio may include evidence of academic writing at level 7 or above, evidence of critical enquiry and critical reasoning, practice reflections, curriculum vitae, attestations/references.\n\r\nInternationals IELTS Score of 7.0 or better in all bands or equivalent and will be required to present a portfolio of evidence that demonstrates best practice in Health and/or Social Practice or related professional context, including the ability to analyse and generate solutions to complex situations.  Must demonstrate a reasonable likelihood of success.\n\r\nAll candidates are required to complete a professional disclosure form and may be required to attend an individual interview.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Certificate in Health and Social Practice will enable practitioners to undertake post qualifying professional development and study on a flexible basis. Students will graduate with a greater capacity to work within specialised fields of practice in health and social services and in leadership, supervision and management roles.  Students will also learn and grow professionally from the inter-disciplinary teaching context and transfer the knowledge to workplace relationships and networks.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Certificate in Health and Social Practice, will have developed knowledge and skills for practice and career progression.  An interdisciplinary context will enable graduates to extend their capacity for critical and professional/clinical reasoning for specialist practice, leadership, management and supervision in complex professional environments.  The Postgraduate Certificate in Health and Social Practice will be relevant to practitioners from a wide range of professional contexts.  Graduates will have developed flexible skills and expertise which will position them well to be responsive to changing social service and health communities.  Learning and participating within the interdisciplinary teaching/learning context will enable graduates to transfer this experience to workplace relationships and networks.\n\r\nThe Postgraduate Certificate in Health and Social Practice is an embedded qualification of the Postgraduate Diploma in Health and Social Practice.","educationPathway":"Graduates of this qualification may apply for entry into the Postgraduate Diploma in Health and Social Practice.","developedBy":"Waikato Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=1768"},"1769":{"i":"1769","entryRequirements":"Undergraduate degree in Health and Social Practice or related discipline, or presentation of a portfolio of evidence to demonstrate best practice in Health and/or Social Practice or related professional context, including the ability to analyse and generate solutions to complex situations.  A Portfolio may include evidence of academic writing at level 7 or above, evidence of critical enquiry and critical reasoning, practice reflections, curriculum vitae, attestations/references.\n\r\nInternationals IELTS Score of 7.0 or better in all bands or equivalent and will be required to present a portfolio of evidence that demonstrates best practice in Health and/or Social Practice or related professional context, including the ability to analyse and generate solutions to complex situations.  Must demonstrate a reasonable likelihood of success.\n\r\nAll candidates are required to complete a professional disclosure form and may be required to attend an individual interview.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Certificate in Professional Supervision will enable practitioners to undertake post qualifying professional development and study on a flexible basis. Students will graduate with a greater capacity to work within specialised fields of practice in health and social services and in leadership, supervision and management roles.  Students will also learn and grow professionally from the inter-disciplinary teaching context and transfer the knowledge to workplace relationships and networks.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Certificate in Professional Supervision, will have developed knowledge and skills for practice and career progression in supervision.  An interdisciplinary context will enable graduates to extend their capacity for critical and professional/clinical reasoning for specialist practice, leadership, management and supervision in complex professional environments.  The Postgraduate Certificate in Professional Supervision will be relevant to practitioners from a wide range of professional contexts.  Graduates will have developed flexible skills and expertise which will position them well to be responsive to changing social service and health communities.  Learning and participating within the interdisciplinary teaching/learning context will enable graduates to transfer this experience to workplace relationships and networks. \n\r\nThe Postgraduate Certificate in Professional Supervision is an embedded qualification of the Postgraduate Diploma in Health and Social Practice.","educationPathway":"Graduates of this qualification may apply for entry into the Postgraduate Diploma in Health and Social Practice.","developedBy":"Waikato Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=1769"},"2039":{"i":"2039","entryRequirements":"Application Criteria: \n\r\nLimitation on places. Entry to the programme is limited by the number of places available.  These places may be apportioned between different categories of eligibility and modes of study. A minimum of one year full time post registration experience and so thus one year in clinical practice at the discretion of the programme manager is required. \n\r\nThe normal requirement for entry is an undergraduate degree in Health Science nursing and or midwifery. It is expected that applicants will be in current clinical practice. 0.4 full-time equivalent position is the expected minimum.  However, applicants who are unable to meet this will be assessed by the postgraduate programme co ordinator to ensure they have appropriate clinical placements. \n\r\nWhere an applicant does not hold an undergraduate degree in Health Science, nursing and or midwifery evidence of extensive professional practice and scholarly achievement to the equivalent of a Bachelor's degree is to be presented in a curriculum vitae accompanied by a statement about advanced practice and postgraduate goals for the future.  \n\r\nAll candidates, both international and permanent residents of New Zealand, from countries where English is not the primary spoken language, require satisfactory achievement of tertiary studies in a country where English is the language of instruction, \n\n\n\r\nOr \n\n\n\r\nIELTS Academic English language test overall score of 7 that includes a score of at least 7 in Reading, Listening, Writing and Speaking.   \n\n\n\r\nWhere preparation is sought for advanced nursing practice, the applicant must also \n\r\nbe a registered nurse \n\r\nhold a current practising certificate \n\r\ndemonstrate specialty nursing practice competencies within a defined scope of practice.   \n\n\n\r\nAll enrolments in the Postgraduate Certificate in Health Science are at the discretion of the Academic and Relationship Manager  in consultation with the Programme Manager and Head of Faculty as required. \n\n\n\r\nSelection Criteria \n\n\n\r\nRight of entry into programmes of study is restricted by SIT and apparent eligibility may not lead to automatic acceptance. Applicants must demonstrate attributes, which in the assessment of SIT should lead to success. \n\n\n\r\nWhere SIT is satisfied that it is necessary to do so because of insufficiency of staff, accommodation or equipment it may determine the maximum number of students who may be enrolled in a particular course of study.  Where the number of applications for enrolment exceeds the number of places in any case where such a limitation applies, the criteria for selection shall be academic merit and suitability for admission to that course of study.  Eligible students not admitted to their chosen course of study will be placed on a waiting list and/or may be referred to another programme.  Applications should be received by SIT no later than the applications due date.  Late applications may be considered, subject to availability of places.","strategicPurposeStatement":"To enable Registered Nurses and/or Midwives to develop skills of research, critical analysis, constructive synthesis and advanced practice in their discipline.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of this programme will articulate their scope of nursing practice and its advancement, work collaboratively across settings and within interdisciplinary environments, show effective nursing leadership , develop and influence health/socioeconomic policies and nursing practice at a local and national level, and show scholarly research inquiry into nursing practice.","developedBy":"Southern Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=2039"},"2285":{"i":"2285","entryRequirements":"Minimum academic entry criteria are: \n\r\nĀkonga entering this programme must hold a bachelor's degree  in an allied health profession, or a profession aligned with allied health with a health and/or wellbeing focus. \n\n\n\r\nInternational applicants for whom English is a second language are required to have an IELTS overall band score (Academic) of 6.5 with a minimum score of 6.5 in each band. These IELTS scores align with what is required in to apply for registration as an occupational therapist in Aotearoa New Zealand. \n\n\n\r\nApplicants who do not meet the academic requirements for entry into the programme can make an application to the Head of School, who will consider the application on a case-by-case basis. Entry to the programme will be at the Head of School's discretion. \n\r\nSelection Criteria* Ākonga who meet the entry criteria will be offered places in order of acceptance to the programme, until all places are full. They will then be placed on a waiting list and informed if a place becomes available.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The aim of the Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Practice in Health and Wellbeing (Specialty) is to produce evidence based health and wellbeing practitioner graduates who are able to use current research to lead advancements in their career, team and/or profession. They will also be able to critically analyse advanced theoretical and/or professional knowledge and apply this to their profession and setting.","graduateProfile":"By the end of this programme, graduates will be able to:  \n\r\n- Critically evaluate relevant literature to improve the effectiveness of practice in Aotearoa New Zealand's bicultural context  \n\r\n- Critically review research methods to support their own and others' practice developments  \n\r\n- Critically analyse practice problems from different perspectives  \n\r\n- Generate solutions to complex problems  \n\r\n- Demonstrate evidence of advanced knowledge in a specialist field or professional practice.","educationPathway":"Graduates will be able to pathway into further postgraduate study.","developedBy":"Otago Polytechnic","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=2285"},"2813":{"i":"2813","entryRequirements":"5.2.1 Entry to the Master of Health Science programme may be limited by the number of places available. \n\r\n5.2.2 The academic entry requirement for the Master of Health Science is one of the following: \n\r\n* an NZQCF-listed Bachelor's or higher level degree (or equivalent) in a health-related field with a minimum of the equivalent to a B- average as per the EIT-specified 11-point achievement-based grading system; \n\r\nor \n\r\n* a degree or equivalent professional qualification in a different field if the applicant can supply evidence of work experience at degree level or above within a health related field, subject to an interview and/or the submission of a portfolio of evidence to establish the status and relevance of the applicant's prior learning and experience; \n\r\nor \n\r\n* completion of the Postgraduate Certificate in Health Science with a minimum B average; \n\r\nor \n\r\n* at the Dean's discretion, where an applicant's situation is compelling but not covered by the requirements listed above. \n\r\n5.2.3 Applicants must demonstrate an acceptable level of English language fluency prior to acceptance in the programme. Ways in which English language fluency may be demonstrated include (i) completion of a programme of study in which English was the language of instruction (conditions apply*), and (ii) approved scores on IELTS tests, namely an Academic score of 6.5 with no band lower than 6 (or accepted international equivalents). \n\r\n5.2.4 An international student must be in possession of an appropriate visa for the duration of the Programme.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Can be completed by coursework, or a combination of coursework and either a project or research. The Master of Health Science provides the opportunity for health practitioners to advance and expand their knowledge and scholarship within an interdisciplinary learning environment. Students will develop skills of research, critical analysis, constructive synthesis and advanced practice within their discipline area; extend their interdisciplinary knowledge; and advance their appreciation and capabilities for collaboration. The programme offers the opportunity for students to reflect on the needs of their clients/patients within the contemporary health care setting that focuses on the integration of care.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Master of Health Science will have advanced knowledge within their specialist field of health science, and will be able to apply that knowledge to new problems and situations in the management and provision of health care. Master of Health Science graduates will demonstrate advanced understandings of population health and health disparities. They will have extended their appreciation of the perspectives of other health professionals and of the contribution of interdisciplinary teams to health care, and will be able to apply this knowledge to planning, implementation and management of health care programmes and services that contribute to health care quality, equity and accessibility. They will be able to research, critically analyse and put forward sound arguments from evidence.","educationPathway":"A doctorate qualification.","developedBy":"Eastern Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=2813"},"2829":{"i":"2829","entryRequirements":"Bachelor's degree or equivalent; English language requirements for EAL applicants: IELTS 7.0 Academic in all bands, Registered nurse or allied health professional, currently employed at least 0.6 FTE within the specialty area.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The programme has been designed for experienced health professionals to support development of enhanced leadership abilities to better meet the health needs of populations within the New Zealand context. The successful graduate of this programme will have advanced practice and leadership capability within their scope of practice.     \n\r\nEach endorsement contributes to the Government's objectives for the tertiary education and health sectors in relationship to their specific/specialty population. The endorsed programme also contributes to the New Zealand Health Strategy aims to ensure that halth workers meet the demand for services that integrate cultural practices, concepts and diverse world views into high-quality, evidence informed health services.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the qualification will have: \n\r\n1.Advanced knowledge and critical understanding of contemporary practice and service delivery issues and strategic policy priorities as they relate to people's health and well-being. \n\r\n2.The ability to review and judiciously utilise research to advocate for best practice innovation which challenges poor population health outcomes. \n\r\n3.The ability to recognise gaps in practice knowledge and to seek solutions to complex and unpredictable health issues within policy, funding, and service delivery parameters. \n\r\n4.Leadership and management skills that are able to be applied in operational and local contexts. \n\r\n5.A sophisticated knowledge of the way power relations can operate to marginalise minority perspectives and to become an informed advocate for equitable access to culturally appropriate and ethical health care for populations.","educationPathway":"Graduates may progress to: \n\r\n - the Whitireia and WelTec Master of Professional Practice  \n\r\n - other master's programmes in Aotearoa New Zealand or overseas","developedBy":"New Zealand Institute of Skills and Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=2829"},"3339":{"i":"3339","entryRequirements":"Students must: * Be able to access a relevant workplace; and * Have a Bachelor degree or Graduate Certificate or Graduate Diploma in a cognate subject; or * Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Professional Studies (with or without endorsement) or in cognate subject for entry to the Postgraduate Diploma; or * A combination of academic and practical or professional experience based upon a record of learning (academic transcript), parchment and a curriculum vitae detailing relevant educational achievements work experience and professional achievements as follows: EITHER * completion of a post-secondary school diploma in a related discipline at NZQA level 7 or equivalent from a recognised tertiary provider; and * demonstration of at least two years relevant practical experience with at least two written references (employer and character); or * demonstration of at least five years relevant practical or professional experience at a senior level, evidence of ability to study at postgraduate qualification level and two written references (employer and character); * IELTS Academic 6.5 with no band score lower than 6.0, or equivalent or Waiariki English Test 65 with no score lower than 60 for Mentoring and Leadership and Adult Teaching endorsements; or * IELTS Academic 7.0 with no band score lower than 7.0, or equivalent or Waiariki English Test 70 with no score lower than 70 for Vulnerable Peoples, and Infection Prevention and Control endorsements.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Professional Studies programme will enable learners to further their knowledge and professional practice in their field of practice. Students will be able to apply an advanced body of knowledge in a range of contexts that will compliment their current experience and/or qualifications. This qualification enables professionals in leadership roles to maintain currency and develop their discipline by ongoing professional development.","graduateProfile":"Upon successful completion of the Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Professional Studies, graduates will be able to: * Supervise and mentor others in their field of study; * Communicate effectively in an inter and intracultural environment; * Work across interdisciplinary boundaries; * Critically evaluate existing research; * Use research to solve problems; and * Work as reflective practitioners.","educationPathway":"The Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Professional Studies is specifically aimed to prepare graduates for roles as team leaders, researchers, practitioners.","developedBy":"Toi Ohomai Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3339"},"3348":{"i":"3348","entryRequirements":"Students must:\n\r\n* Be able to access a relevant workplace; and\n\r\n* Have a Bachelor degree or Graduate Certificate or Graduate Diploma in a cognate subject; or\n\r\n* Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Professional Studies (with or without endorsement) or in\n\r\ncognate subject for entry to the Postgraduate Diploma; or\n\r\n* A combination of academic and practical or professional experience based upon a record of\n\r\nlearning (academic transcript), parchment and a curriculum vitae detailing relevant\n\r\neducational achievements work experience and professional achievements as follows:\n\r\nEITHER\n\r\n* completion of a post-secondary school diploma in a related discipline at NZQA level 7 or\n\r\nequivalent from a recognised tertiary provider; and\n\r\n* demonstration of at least two years relevant practical experience with at least two written\n\r\nreferences (employer and character); or\n\r\n* demonstration of at least five years relevant practical or professional experience at a\n\r\nsenior level, evidence of ability to study at postgraduate qualification level and two written\n\r\nreferences (employer and character);\n\r\n* IELTS Academic 6.5 with no band score lower than 6.0, or equivalent or Waiariki English Test\n\r\n65 with no score lower than 60 for Mentoring and Leadership and Adult Teaching\n\r\nendorsements; or\n\r\n* IELTS Academic 7.0 with no band score lower than 7.0, or equivalent or Waiariki English Test\n\r\n70 with no score lower than 70 for Vulnerable Peoples, and Infection Prevention and Control\n\r\nendorsements.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Professional Studies will enable learners to critically\n\r\nexamine theories and models of continuing development through leadership. Students will have\n\r\nthe opportunity to exhibit advanced knowledge and expertise in professional leadership in the\n\r\ncontext of their specialist field which compliments their current experience and/or qualifications.\n\r\nThis qualification enables professionals in leadership roles to maintain currency and to critique\n\r\ntheir leadership practice.","graduateProfile":"Upon successful completion of the Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Professional Studies,\n\r\ngraduates will be able to:\n\r\n* Develop pedagogical content expertise within their field of study;\n\r\n* Critically evaluate their personal practice;\n\r\n* Critique challenges and issues within their specialist field and use to solve problems;\n\r\n* Operate within their communities of practice;\n\r\n* Advocate for self and others.","educationPathway":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Professional Studies will be eligible for entry\n\r\nto the Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Professional Studies programme or further Postgraduate\n\r\nstudy.","developedBy":"Toi Ohomai Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3348"},"3354":{"i":"3354","entryRequirements":"Students must: * Be able to access a relevant workplace; and * Have a Bachelor degree or Graduate Certificate or Graduate Diploma in a cognate subject; or * Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Professional Studies (with or without endorsement) or in cognate subject for entry to the Postgraduate Diploma; or * A combination of academic and practical or professional experience based upon a record of learning (academic transcript), parchment and a curriculum vitae detailing relevant educational achievements work experience and professional achievements as follows: EITHER * completion of a post-secondary school diploma in a related discipline at NZQA level 7 or equivalent from a recognised tertiary provider; and * demonstration of at least two years relevant practical experience with at least two written references (employer and character); or * demonstration of at least five years relevant practical or professional experience at a senior level, evidence of ability to study at postgraduate qualification level and two written references (employer and character); * IELTS Academic 6.5 with no band score lower than 6.0, or equivalent or Waiariki English Test 65 with no score lower than 60 for Mentoring and Leadership and Adult Teaching endorsements; or * IELTS Academic 7.0 with no band score lower than 7.0, or equivalent or Waiariki English Test 70 with no score lower than 70 for Vulnerable Peoples, and Infection Prevention and Control endorsements.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Professional Studies will enable learners to critically examine theories and models of continuing development through leadership. Students will have the opportunity to exhibit advanced knowledge and expertise in professional leadership in the context of their specialist field which compliments their current experience and/or qualifications. This qualification enables professionals in leadership roles to maintain currency and to critique their leadership practice.","graduateProfile":"Upon successful completion of the Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Professional Studies, graduates will be able to: * Develop pedagogical content expertise within their field of study; * Critically evaluate their personal practice; * Critique challenges and issues within their specialist field and use to solve problems; * Operate within their communities of practice; * Advocate for self and others.","educationPathway":"The Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Professional Studies is specifically aimed to prepare graduates for roles as team leaders, researchers, practitioners.","developedBy":"Toi Ohomai Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3354"},"3373":{"i":"3373","entryRequirements":"The Master of Applied Professional Studies is specifically aimed to prepare graduates for leadership roles and becoming advanced practitioners in their relevant field of study. Entry Requirements: Students must: * Be able to access a relevant workplace; and * Have a Bachelor or Bachelor Honours degree in a cognate subject with a B average or above; or * Have a Postgraduate Certificate or Postgraduate Diploma in a cognate subject with a B average or above; or * In exceptional circumstances, based on academic merit and relevant experience, students who do not meet the academic and practical or professional experience requirements above may be considered for admission subject to the completion of any qualifying courses the Postgraduate Board of Studies may prescribe which must be completed either prior to or concurrently; and have * IELTS Academic 6.5 with no band score lower than 6.0, or equivalent or Waiariki English Test 65 with no score lower than 60 for Mentoring and Leadership and Adult Teaching endorsements; or * IELTS Academic 7.0 with no band score lower than 7.0, or equivalent or Waiariki English Test 70 with no score lower than 70 for Vulnerable Peoples, and Infection Prevention and Control endorsements.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Master of Applied Professional Studies programme aims to provide a flexible range of study options that enable learners to match their needs to the qualification they are seeking to gain and to extend their domain of practice within a chosen professional field. The programme aims to integrate theory with practice within interrogative environments that support learners to broaden their knowledge and experience through: * Reflective practice * Critical evaluation * In-depth analysis of critical social, cultural and professional practice issues * Applied professional practice research * Synthesis and construction of new and/or innovative professional practice initiatives and/or applications * Articulation of personalised professional practice model(s) along with the theories, cultural understandings and experiences that inform the model(s)","graduateProfile":"Upon successful completion of the Master of Applied Professional Studies, graduates will be able to: * Perform as critically reflective and interdisciplinary practitioners; * Demonstrate leadership in their field of study nationally and internationally; * Analyse and synthesise information; * Use and apply knowledge to address novel or new problems and issues; * Develop and implement appropriate research methodologies; and * Exhibit higher level knowledge and understanding of their profession through cognitive, practical, personal and enabling skills.","educationPathway":"Graduates of the Master of Applied Professional Studies will be eligible for entry to other\n\r\nPostgraduate studies or a Doctoral degree.","developedBy":"Toi Ohomai Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3373"},"3650":{"i":"3650","entryRequirements":"Students will have completed all requirements of a bachelor's degree or graduate diploma in a relevant field (such as chiropractic, health Sciences, massage therapy, medicine, naturopathy, nursing, occupational therapy, osteopathy, physiotherapy, sport, and exercise) with at least a 70-74% average at Level 7 or a B grade average.   \n\r\nTo proceed to a Master of Applied Health Sciences (Wellness and Rehabilitation) from the Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Health Sciences (Wellness and Rehabilitation) or equivalent programme, applicants will be expected to have achieved a 70-70% grade or higher on average in that programme of study. All postgraduate diploma level papers must be at Level 8 or above.  \n\n\n\r\nSpecial Admission  \n\n\n\r\nNotwithstanding the above admission criteria, in exceptional circumstances, a mature aged applicant who can show evidence of ability to succeed in the programmes may be considered for admission, provided the applicant has successfully completed an approved course or programme, or has relevant industry experience, which is deemed to meet the required standard for entry.  \n\n\n\r\nProvisional Part-time Admission  \n\n\n\r\nAn applicant who does not meet academic criteria may be provisionally admitted to enrol in one or more papers. Upon successful completion of the paper(s), the student may apply for special admission.  \n\r\nApplicants from countries with an annual student visa approval rate of at least 80 per cent, whose first language is not English, or who come from a country where the language of instruction in schools is not English, are required to provide evidence of having passed an NZQA approved internal English Language Assessment, or one of the following tests of English language competence in accordance with the NZQA rules below  \n\n\n\r\nIELTS test - Academic score of 6.5 with no band score lower than 6  \n\r\nTOEFL Paper based test (pBT) - Score of 590 (with an essay score 5.5 TWE)  \n\r\nTOEFL Internet- based test (iBT) - Score of 79 (with a writing score of 21)  \n\r\nUniversity of Cambridge ESOL Examinations - CAE or CPE with a score of 176. No less than 169 in each skill.  \n\r\nNZCEL - Level 5 with the Academic endorsement  \n\r\nPearson Test of English (Academic) - PToE (Academic score of 58)  \n\r\nCity of Guilds IESOL - C1 Expert with a score of 42  \n\n\n\r\nApplicants from countries with an annual student visa approval rate below 80 per cent, whose first language is not English, or who come from a country where the language of instruction in schools is not English must provide evidence that they  \n\n\n\r\nHave gained NCEA Level 3 and met New Zealand University Entrance requirements or  \n\r\nHold a bachelor's degree of at least 3 years from New Zealand, Australia, Canada, The Republic of Ireland, South Africa, United Kingdom or United States of America or  \n\r\nHave achieved a Certificate in English Language Teaching to Adults, CELTA or  \n\r\nHave achieved one of the English Language competence tests specified above  \n\n\n\r\nAll enrolments in the Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Health Sciences (Wellness and Rehabilitation), Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Health Sciences (Wellness and Rehabilitation) and Master of Applied Health Sciences (Wellness and Rehabilitation) are approved at the discretion of the Programme Manager in consultation with the Head of Faculty and teaching staff as required. The Head of Faculty will determine the maximum number of students permitted to enrol in the postgraduate programme.  \n\n\n\r\nApplicants may be required to attend an interview, or if they live at some distance from the campus, complete a telephone interview. Applicants may be required to provide copies of applicable certificates and evidence of previous achievements prior to the interview date.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Master of Applied Health Sciences (Wellness and Rehabilitation) is aimed at wellness and rehabilitation practitioners and recent graduates (in fields such as chiropractic, health Sciences, massage therapy, medicine, naturopathy, nursing, occupational therapy, osteopathy, physiotherapy, sport, and exercise) wishing to undertake an advanced programme of study in order to prepare for further study or to assist with obtaining a more senior position. The programme will enable them to extend their capability in critical and professional/clinical reasoning for specialist practice, leadership, and management in professional settings.    \n\r\nThe programme is tailored to the individual study needs of each student. Public and private sector organisation's employing graduates of the Master of Applied Health Sciences (Wellness and Rehabilitation) will benefit from the advanced knowledge and capabilities (including analytical and research) that the graduates have acquired during their programme of study","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Master of Applied Health Sciences (Wellness and Rehabilitation) will be able to   \n\n\n\r\nset and justify priorities, solve complex problems using credible evidence in novel environments, and organise and manage resources related to wellness and rehabilitation or performance   \n\n\n\r\ndesign, carry out and communicate the results of significant research projects in the field of wellness and rehabilitation and relate the findings to the professional and research literature   \n\n\n\r\nanalyse and critique professional and research publications in wellness, rehabilitation and related subject areas, identify practical applications and relate findings to their own research   \n\n\n\r\napply their analytical and research capabilities to unfamiliar situations involving the application of wellness and rehabilitation practices   \n\n\n\r\nresearch, integrate and apply advanced understanding of wellness and rehabilitation approaches, assessment, training and methodology   \n\r\ndemonstrate high levels of skill as a wellness and rehabilitation practitioner or in a research role in an organisation    \n\n\n\r\nthink critically and act responsibly when confronted with academic or professional challenges","educationPathway":"Graduates of this programme may seek entry to doctorate programmes of study.","developedBy":"Southern Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3650"},"3651":{"i":"3651","entryRequirements":"Admission criteria for the Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Health Sciences (Wellness and Rehabilitation) are as follows: \n\r\nStudents will have completed all requirements of a bachelor's degree or graduate diploma in a relevant field (such as chiropractic, health science, massage therapy, medicine, naturopathy, nursing, occupational therapy, osteopathy, physiotherapy, sport and exercise) with at least a B grade average at level 7 \n\n\n\r\nSpecial Admission \n\n\n\r\nNotwithstanding the above admission criteria, in exceptional circumstances, a mature aged applicant who can show evidence of ability to succeed in the programmes may be considered for admission, provided the applicant has successfully completed an approved course or programme, or has relevant industry experience, which is deemed to meet the required standard for entry. \n\n\n\r\nProvisional Part-time Admission \n\n\n\r\nAn applicant who does not meet academic criteria may be provisionally admitted to enrol in one or more papers. Upon successful completion of the paper(s), the student may apply for special admission. \n\r\nApplicants from countries with an annual student visa approval rate of at least 80 per cent, whose first language is not English, or who come from a country where the language of instruction in schools is not English, are required to provide evidence of having passed an NZQA approved internal English Language Assessment, or one of the following tests of English language competence in accordance with the NZQA rules below \n\n\n\r\nIELTS test - Academic score of 6.5 with no band score lower than 6 \n\r\nTOEFL Paper based test (pBT) - Score of 590 (with an essay score 5.5 TWE) \n\r\nTOEFL Internet- based test (iBT) - Score of 79 (with a writing score of 21) \n\r\nUniversity of Cambridge ESOL Examinations - CAE or CPE with a score of 176. No less than 169 in each skill. \n\r\nNZCEL - Level 5 with the Academic endorsement \n\r\nPearson Test of English (Academic) - PToE (Academic score of 58) \n\r\nCity of Guilds IESOL - C1 Expert with a score of 42 \n\n\n\r\nApplicants from countries with an annual student visa approval rate below 80 per cent, whose first language is not English, or who come from a country where the language of instruction in schools is not English must provide evidence that they \n\n\n\r\nHave gained NCEA Level 3 and met New Zealand University Entrance requirements or \n\r\nHold a bachelor's degree of at least 3 years from New Zealand, Australia, Canada, The Republic of Ireland, South Africa, United Kingdom or United States of America or \n\r\nHave achieved a Certificate in English Language Teaching to Adults, CELTA or \n\r\nHave achieved one of the English Language competence tests specified above \n\n\n\r\nAll enrolments in the Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Health Sciences (Wellness and Rehabilitation), Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Health Sciences (Wellness and Rehabilitation) and Master of Applied Health Sciences (Wellness and Rehabilitation) are approved at the discretion of the Programme Manager in consultation with the Head of Faculty and teaching staff as required. The Head of Faculty will determine the maximum number of students permitted to enrol in the postgraduate programme. \n\n\n\r\nApplicants may be required to attend an interview, or if they live at some distance from the campus, complete a telephone interview. Applicants may be required to provide copies of applicable certificates and evidence of previous achievements prior to the interview date.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Health Science (Wellness and Rehabilitation) is aimed at wellness and rehabilitation practitioners wishing to undertake a short programme of study in order to extend and update their knowledge and skills. The programme is tailored to the individual study needs of each student. Public and private sector organisation's employing graduates of the Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Health Science (Wellness and Rehabilitation) will benefit from the knowledge and specialist skills that the graduates have acquired during their programme of study.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Health Science (Wellness and Rehabilitation) will be able to  \n\r\nrecognize cultural differences and ethical issues, and consult and collaborate with other health professionals  \n\r\nassess wellness and rehabilitation needs of clients and determine appropriate responses  \n\r\nshow evidence of advanced knowledge about wellness and rehabilitation  \n\r\napply acquired knowledge and skills in practical situations  \n\r\nevaluate evidence in order to support a course of action.","educationPathway":"Graduates of this programme may seek entry to doctorate programmes of study.","developedBy":"Southern Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3651"},"3652":{"i":"3652","entryRequirements":"Admission criteria for the Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Health  \n\r\nSciences (Wellness and Rehabilitation) are as follows: \n\r\nStudents will have completed all requirements of a bachelor's degree or graduate diploma in a relevant field (such as chiropractic, health science, massage therapy, medicine, naturopathy, nursing, occupational therapy, osteopathy, physiotherapy, sport and exercise) with at least a B grade average at level 7. To proceed to the Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Health Sciences (Wellness and Rehabilitation) from the Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Health Sciences (Wellness and Rehabilitation) or equivalent programme, applicants will be expected to have achieved at least a B grade average in that programme of study. \n\n\n\r\nSpecial Admission \n\n\n\r\nNotwithstanding the above admission criteria, in exceptional circumstances, a mature aged applicant who can show evidence of ability to succeed in the programmes may be considered for admission, provided the applicant has successfully completed an approved course or programme, or has relevant industry experience, which is deemed to meet the required standard for entry. \n\n\n\r\nProvisional Part-time Admission \n\n\n\r\nAn applicant who does not meet academic criteria may be provisionally admitted to enrol in one or more papers. Upon successful completion of the paper(s), the student may apply for special admission. \n\r\nApplicants from countries with an annual student visa approval rate of at least 80 per cent, whose first language is not English, or who come from a country where the language of instruction in schools is not English, are required to provide evidence of having passed an NZQA approved internal English Language Assessment, or one of the following tests of English language competence in accordance with the NZQA rules below \n\n\n\r\nIELTS test - Academic score of 6.5 with no band score lower than 6 \n\r\nTOEFL Paper based test (pBT) - Score of 590 (with an essay score 5.5 TWE) \n\r\nTOEFL Internet- based test (iBT) - Score of 79 (with a writing score of 21) \n\r\nUniversity of Cambridge ESOL Examinations - CAE or CPE with a score of 176. No less than 169 in each skill. \n\r\nNZCEL - Level 5 with the Academic endorsement \n\r\nPearson Test of English (Academic) - PToE (Academic score of 58) \n\r\nCity of Guilds IESOL - C1 Expert with a score of 42 \n\n\n\r\nApplicants from countries with an annual student visa approval rate below 80 per cent, whose first language is not English, or who come from a country where the language of instruction in schools is not English must provide evidence that they \n\n\n\r\nHave gained NCEA Level 3 and met New Zealand University Entrance requirements or \n\r\nHold a bachelor's degree of at least 3 years from New Zealand, Australia, Canada, The Republic of Ireland, South Africa, United Kingdom or United States of America or \n\r\nHave achieved a Certificate in English Language Teaching to Adults, CELTA or \n\r\nHave achieved one of the English Language competence tests specified above \n\n\n\r\nAll enrolments in the Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Health Sciences (Wellness and Rehabilitation), Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Health Sciences (Wellness and Rehabilitation) and Master of Applied Health Sciences (Wellness and Rehabilitation) are approved at the discretion of the Programme Manager in consultation with the Head of Faculty and teaching staff as required. The Head of Faculty will determine the maximum number of students permitted to enrol in the postgraduate programme. \n\n\n\r\nApplicants may be required to attend an interview, or if they live at some distance from the campus, complete a telephone interview. Applicants may be required to provide copies of applicable certificates and evidence of previous achievements prior to the interview date.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Health Science (Wellness and Rehabilitation) is aimed at wellness and rehabilitation practitioners and recent graduates (in fields such as chiropractic, health science, massage therapy, medicine, naturopathy, nursing, occupational therapy, osteopathy, physiotherapy, sport and exercise) wishing to undertake a comprehensive programme of study in order to upgrade their qualifications and extend their knowledge and skills with the objective of obtaining employment or advancing their careers. The programme is tailored to the individual study needs of each student. Public and private sector organisations employing graduates of the Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Health Science (Wellness and Rehabilitation) will benefit from the broad knowledge and skill set (including problem-solving) that the graduates have acquired during their programme of study.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Health Science (Wellness and Rehabilitation) will be able to  \n\n\n\r\ndemonstrate mastery of complex concepts and theories in the field of wellness and rehabilitation and their application in solving practical problems  \n\n\n\r\nprescribe, monitor and critically evaluate wellness and rehabilitative programmes using a client-centred approach within their own discipline   \n\n\n\r\ncritique and reflect on personal specialty practices and take responsibility for clients' needs  \n\n\n\r\nshow evidence of advanced knowledge about specialist areas of wellness and rehabilitation  \n\n\n\r\ngather, evaluate and analyse information from a variety of sources","educationPathway":"Graduates of this programme may seek entry to doctorate programmes of study.","developedBy":"Southern Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3652"},"3704":{"i":"3704","entryRequirements":"Minimum entry requirements are \n\r\n1. The Bachelor of Applied Science (Level 7), or an equivalent qualification at bachelor level in a related discipline, or equivalent documented professional experience.  \n\r\n2. International learners are also required to achieve a minimum overall IELTS (Academic) score of 6.5, with no band score less than 6.0, from one test taken in the preceding two years, or equivalent.   \n\n\n\r\nAdditional criteria \n\r\nAll applicants who are accepted must obtain a First Aid Certificate, and complete the requirements of the Vulnerable Children's Act 2014 (including police vetting), prior to commencing classes.","strategicPurposeStatement":"To produce graduates who can extend and deepen their knowledge and understanding of the underpinning base theories and procedures that are relevant to the practice environment. Graduates will have completed an applied project, which allows them to address their practice from multiple perspectives and to position their practice within a wider industry context. This qualification prepares learners for further postgraduate study or a career in sport or exercise.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Science will be able to:  \n\r\na. Work independently to integrate skills, techniques and ideas associated with their area of practice within an applied industry setting \n\r\nb. Analyse a range of information and incorporate critique to arrive at a resolved position within their area of practice \n\r\nc. Reflect on the application of professional practice in a workplace environment \n\r\nd. Integrate sustainability from cultural, social, environmental and economic perspectives \n\r\ne. Apply skills, technologies, techniques and ideas within an applied industry setting \n\r\nf. Evaluate how their work is positioned in a wider context \n\r\ng. Assess and evaluate the cultural, social, environmental and economic impact of their practice and the practice of others","educationPathway":"It is expected that graduates of the Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Science will be able to gain entry into further postgraduate level qualifications at tertiary institutions (dependant on meeting programme-specific entry criteria). Possible programmes include the Master of Applied Science or the Master of Professional Practice at Otago Polytechnic; Master of Public Health, Physical Education or Teaching at the University of Otago; Master of Sport and Exercise, Public Health or Health Science at Massey University; or Master of Health Sciences or Science at the University of Auckland.","developedBy":"Otago Polytechnic","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3704"},"3705":{"i":"3705","entryRequirements":"Minimum entry requirements are \n\r\n1. The Bachelor of Applied Science (Level 7), or an equivalent qualification at bachelor level in a related discipline, or equivalent documented professional experience.  \n\r\n2. International learners are also required to achieve a minimum overall IELTS (Academic) score of 6.5, with no band score less than 6.0, from one test taken in the preceding two years, or equivalent.   \n\n\n\r\nAdditional criteria \n\r\nAll applicants who are accepted must obtain a First Aid Certificate, and complete the requirements of the Vulnerable Children's Act 2014 (including police vetting), prior to commencing classes.","strategicPurposeStatement":"To produce graduates who can extend and deepen their knowledge of the underpinning base theories and procedures used in the practice environment, in a wider and more encompassing scope than a postgraduate certificate, including a greater understanding of the roles of those who are working with them. Graduates will have completed an applied project, which allows them to address their practice from multiple perspectives and to position their practice within a wider industry context. This qualification prepares learners for further postgraduate study or a career in advanced sport or exercise.","graduateProfile":"Graduate Profile:  \n\r\n(Outcome) Graduates of the Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Science will be able to:  \n\r\na. Work independently to integrate skills, techniques and ideas associated with their area of practice within an applied industry setting \n\r\nb. Evaluate the historical and contemporary conventions of their field and describe how this has impacted on practice now \n\r\nc. Analyse sophisticated information and incorporate critique to arrive at a resolved position within their area of practice \n\r\nd. Reflect on the application of professional practice in a workplace environment \n\r\ne. Produce a proposal-based body of critically engaged applied sport/exercise/health research  \n\r\nf. Integrate sustainability from cultural, social, environmental and/or economic perspectives \n\r\ng. Assess and evaluate the cultural, social, environmental and/or economic impact of a project  \n\r\nh. Produce a scholarly research document or equivalent that supports a chosen project \n\r\ni. Evaluate and articulate how their work is positioned within a wider context \n\r\nj. Exhibit or present their project in a public forum","educationPathway":"It is expected that graduates of the Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Science will be able to gain entry into master level qualifications at tertiary institutions (dependant on meeting programme-specific entry criteria). Possible programmes include the Master of Applied Science or the Master of Professional Practice at Otago Polytechnic; Master of Public Health, Physical Education or Teaching at the University of Otago; Master of Sport and Exercise, Public Health or Health Science at Massey University; or Master of Health Sciences or Science at the University of Auckland.","developedBy":"Otago Polytechnic","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3705"},"3706":{"i":"3706","entryRequirements":"Minimum entry requirements are \n\r\n1. Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Science at level 8, or equivalent, with an overall grade of B+ (75%), for admission to the Masters by Research;  \n\r\nOr  \n\r\nPostgraduate Diploma in Applied Science at level 8, or equivalent, with an overall grade of B+ in the final 60 credits, or an equivalent postgraduate qualification of 120 credits in a related area with an overall grade of B+, for admission to the Masters by coursework.  \n\r\n2. International learners must achieve a minimum overall IELTS (Academic) score of 6.5, with no individual band less than 6.0, or equivalent, from one test taken in the preceding two years, or equivalent.  \n\n\n\r\nExceptional applicants not meeting the qualification requirements, but who have appropriate documented professional experience, may also be considered for admission. \n\n\n\r\nAdditional criteria \n\r\nAll applicants who are accepted must obtain a First Aid Certificate, and complete the requirements of the Vulnerable Children's Act 2014 (including police vetting), prior to commencing classes.","strategicPurposeStatement":"To produce graduates who can independently demonstrate mastery of theoretically and procedurally sophisticated subject matter through a body of scholarly applied work, which is presented in a public forum and supported by a project or thesis, which could form the basis of scholarly journal articles. The work will respond to societal needs, address practice from multiple perspectives and be positioned within a wider framework of academic and applied research. This qualification prepares learners for doctoral level study, an academic career or a lead sport or exercise management role.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Master of Applied Science will be able to:  \n\r\na. Demonstrate mastery of skills, techniques and methods associated with their discipline \n\r\nb. Analyse sophisticated information and incorporate critique to arrive at a resolved final industry outcome or thesis \n\r\nc. Integrate sustainability from cultural, social, environmental and/or economic perspectives through the body of creative work OR thesis \n\r\nd. Assess and evaluate the cultural, social, environmental and economic impact of a project or subject matter \n\r\ne. Present their original work in a local, national or international forum \n\r\nf. Craft sophisticated creative solutions and respond to professional challenges \n\n\n\r\nIn addition, graduates who complete a research component of 90 credits or more in the Master of Applied Science will be able to: \n\r\na. Demonstrate a high order of skill in the planning, execution and completion of a piece of original research or creative scholarly work  \n\r\nb. Apply such skills learned during the study programme to new situations","educationPathway":"It is expected that graduates of the Master of Applied Science will be able to gain entry into doctoral level qualifications at tertiary institutions (dependant on meeting programme-specific entry criteria). Possible programmes include the Doctor of Professional Practice at Otago Polytechnic and PhD programmes at other institutions.","developedBy":"Otago Polytechnic","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3706"},"3729":{"i":"3729","entryRequirements":"Academic Requirements \n\r\nBachelor of Musculoskeletal Health.\n\n\n\r\nAlternative Requirements\n\r\nApplicants who are unable to evidence that they meet Academic Requirements, but who can demonstrate acquired skills for tertiary study gained through study, work and/or life experience, may be approved for alternative entry. This may include Recognition of Prior Learning. Contact Ara for advice.\n\n\n\r\nIf you do not hold the Bachelor of Musculoskeletal Health, you may:\n\r\n* provide evidence of having completed a relevant professional qualification; and\n\r\n* provide evidence of successful completion of a relevant qualification or programme of study which is equivalent to the Bachelor of Musculoskeletal Health, through the submission of a portfolio of evidence.\n\r\nIf your undergraduate degree is not assessed as meeting the full requirements for this programme, enrolment in transitional or undergraduate courses may be required before admission to this programme.\n\n\n\r\nEnglish Requirements\n\r\nIf English is not the applicant's first language, applicants will need to provide a result from a test or qualification on the acceptable alternatives English Proficiency Outcomes Chart. Applicants who do not have evidence of English language skills and are a New Zealand citizen or permanent resident, may contact us for an assessment.\n\r\n* IELTS 6.5 Academic (no lower than 6.5 in any subtest)\n\n\n\r\nNote:\n\r\nThe English Language requirements for this programme are higher than the minimum set by NZQA, therefore; applicants who have achieved NCEA Level 3 University Entrance may be required to provide evidence of English Language skills.\n\r\nIELTS scores used must be taken from a single IELTS Test Report Form and are valid for two years from the date of the test.\n\n\n\r\nAdditional Entry Requirements:\n\r\n* In order to access an individual placement in this programme, the applicant may be required to provide evidence of immunity to particular infectious diseases or other health requirements specific to the practice.\n\n\n\r\n* Consent to Disclosure of Information \n\r\nSuccessful applicants will be required to complete a New Zealand Police Consent to Disclosure of Information form. The form will be sent by Ara to the Police Licensing and Vetting Service and returned in confidence to the Faculty Dean or delegate. Information on the NZ Police Vetting Service is available from the New Zealand Police website.\n\n\n\r\nAdmission\n\r\nApplicants who meet the requirements for admission will be offered a place in the programme.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Diploma will: \n\r\n1. Ensure graduates are competent to apply for registration with the Osteopathic Council of New Zealand to meet the needs of local communities in the provision of primary healthcare. \n\r\n2. Ensure graduates are competent to work in osteopathic practice in New Zealand and understand their limitations and scope of practice boundaries.  \n\r\n3. Enable graduates to enhance the osteopathic profession through an understanding of the need to partner with tangata whenua and tangata Tiriti and demonstrate a commitment to meeting these responsibilities.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Post Graduate Diploma in Osteopathy will be able to:   \n\r\n1. Critically reflect on the responsibilities of te Tiriti o Waitangi by demonstrating cultural responsiveness and a commitment to the provision of equitable culturally responsive health care practices. (Domain 1) \n\r\n2. Apply OCNZ competencies to practice meeting the professional standards required for registration pathways and regulated health practice in Aotearoa NZ. (Domain 1,2,3,4,5). \n\r\n3. Critically examine osteopathic practice, maintaining professional competence, and uphold the principles of health education, disease prevention, and rehabilitation. (Domain 1, 3, 4) \n\r\n4. Operate within the scope of osteopathic practice, integrating and adapting evidence-informed osteopathic clinical science knowledge, skills, techniques and reasoning to person-centred care. (Domain 1, 3) \n\r\n5. Critically reflect and take action to practice in an inclusive, person-centred partnership that enhances mana, promotes cultural responsiveness, and respect diversity, ensuring effective engagement with patients and their  \n\r\nwhānau. (Domain 2) \n\r\n6. Critically reflect on and articulate evidence informed osteopathic philosophy, a professional ethos and rationale for osteopathic practice. (Domain 3, 5).","educationPathway":"Master in Health Science (Ara, AUT, Canterbury, Otago, Auckland), Master of Health Sciences (MHealSc) endorsed in Musculoskeletal Management (Otago), Master of Health Practice in Child Health (AUT), Master of Health Sciences (MHealSc) endorsed in Pain and Pain Management (Otago), Postgraduate Diploma in Health Science in Acupuncture (AUT), Master of Health Practice in Acupuncture (AUT), Postgraduate Certificate in Health Science in Child Health (AUT), Postgraduate Certificate or Diploma in Health Science in Child Health (AUT), Postgraduate Certificate or Diploma in Health Science in Older Adult: Health and Wellness (AUT), Postgraduate Diploma in Health Sciences endorsed in Musculoskeletal Management (University of Otago), Postgraduate Diploma in Health Sciences endorsed in Pain and Pain Management (University of Otago)","developedBy":"Ara Institute of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3729"},"3852":{"i":"3852","entryRequirements":"The academic entry requirement for the Master of Nursing Science is one of the following: * an NZQF-listed Bachelor's or higher degree with a minimum of the equivalent to a B average as per the EIT-specified 11-point achievement-based grading system; or * a nursing qualification deemed equivalent to the above with a minimum of the equivalent to a B average as per the EIT-specified 11-point achievement-based grading system; or * at the Dean's discretion, where an applicant's situation is compelling but not covered by the requirements listed above. All applicants must demonstrate an acceptable level of English language fluency prior to acceptance in the programme. Ways in which international students may demonstrate English language fluency include (i) completion of a programme of study in which English was the language of instruction (conditions apply*), and (ii) approved scores on IELTS tests, namely an Academic score of 6.5 with no band lower than 6 (or accepted international equivalents).","strategicPurposeStatement":"The MNSc aims to enable registered nurses seeking postgraduate study to prepare for a variety of advanced nursing practice and leadership roles, but not that of a Nurse Practitioner, further developing their knowledge and skills for evidence-based practice, clinical specialty practice, advanced nursing practice, research, education and leadership. Graduates of the programme will be equipped with expanded nursing knowledge, refined skills for evidence-based practice, enhanced clinical judgment and research skills, which will enable them to deliver advanced nursing practice and leadership.","graduateProfile":"Critically analyse contemporary disparities and social determinants in health and wellness, and act as leaders in bringing about significant and positive changes in their field of practice;  \n\r\nApply research evidence to existing and emerging problems both independently and collaboratively, relating best practice to advanced contemporary nursing science theory, practice and education;  \n\r\nPropose, initiate and participate in innovative and inter-professional approaches to learning and practice, devising creative solutions to problems and cultivating others' capacity for inquiry;  \n\r\nCritically evaluate the legal, ethical, cultural and political dimensions of the nursing environment, including those specific to Maori, and relate their impact to advanced nursing practice and education;  \n\r\nSynthesise information from a range of contemporary sources, including indigenous knowledge, to conduct, lead and positively impact scientifically based research that influences health policy and leads to improvement in health outcomes among individuals, families/whanau and diverse communities.","educationPathway":"Undergraduate Nursing degree - Postgraduate Diploma in Health Science - Master of Nursing Science  \n\r\nMaster of Nursing Science - Doctoral study","developedBy":"Eastern Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3852"},"3892":{"i":"3892","entryRequirements":"Candidates are required to have:University Entrance (UE) or equivalent is the minimum requirement to enter the Bachelor of Physiotherapy (Honours) programme.  To qualify for entry candidates need NCEA Level 3 comprised of 60 credits at NCEA Level 3 or above and 20 credits at NCEA Level 2 or above,  \n\r\nOR a relevant level 4 qualifiction \n\r\nOR Equivalent","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Wintec Bachelor of Physiotherapy programme differs in several ways from those currently offered in Aotearoa New Zealand. A key aim of this programme, which is strongly linked to the results of an extensive consultation process with industry, is to develop work-ready physiotherapists, equipped to meet the needs of communities across the Midland region, in particular rural and remote communities. Furthermore, we aim to adhere to the nationally mandated aim of the New Zealand Physiotherapy Board, and industry-identified requirement to increase the number of Māori and Pasifika physiotherapists in Aotearoa New Zealand. It is our belief that all practicing physiotherapists in this country should be culturally competent and confident in working with whānau. To achieve these aims, Wintec will implement a recruitment strategy that will support Māori and Pasifika students to enter the programme and has developed a programme that supports the development of practitioners who are well equipped to work with whānau.  \n\r\nAnother aim of our programme is to develop physiotherapists who are competent in interprofessional practice by offering comprehensive and authentic interprofessional teaching and learning and assessment opportunities. This programme has multiple streams of health science students taught the same content together in a classroom. Interprofessional teaching and learning incorporates activities where students from different disciplines learn together about and from each other so each gains appreciation and understanding of other disciplines and professions and how they can work together for the best outcome for the client . \n\r\nThe Wintec programme also differs from those currently offered in its mode of delivery. Wintec's degree is to be offered in flexible mode and content will be delivered in block courses on campus supported by online learning activities in a blended learning approach. Online and face to face learning will follow flipped classroom principles, so that underpinning knowledge is delivered online and then applied practically or theoretically in the physiotherapy contexts in face to face classroom sessions to consolidate knowledge and skills. This mode of delivery will support students to be able to continue to live in their own community without the requirement to relocate to study. Clinical practice can also be undertaken close to home and students will be encouraged to find a physiotherapist mentor to assist them in their studies; bringing them closer to the physiotherapy community in their local area and to facilitate students and graduates into their local workforce","graduateProfile":"A graduate of the Bachelor of Physiotherapy (Honours) will be able to: \n\r\n* Practice professional, ethical and values-based physiotherapy with clients over the lifespan and across clinical settings to enhance the hauora of individuals and communities. (Physiotherapy practitioner, Professional and ethical practitioner)  \n\r\n* Work collaboratively in an interprofessional workforce and engage in inclusive, culturally responsive and person-centred practice.  (Collaborative practitioner) \n\r\n* Demonstrate contemporary applications of Te Tiriti o Waitangi through culturally responsive, holistic and safe physiotherapy care, to engage effectively with whānau in healthcare settings in Aotearoa New Zealand (Physiotherapy practitioner, Professional and ethical practitioner)  \n\r\n* Engage in original rangahau or research, reflect on practice and apply critical thinking and self-directed learning to contribute to the advancement of physiotherapy practice in Aotearoa New Zealand and globally. (Reflective practitioner and self-directed learner, Leader)  \n\r\n* Build and maintain relationships to communicate effectively, advocate for and educate individuals, whānau, health professionals and other stakeholders (Communicator, Educator)","educationPathway":"Graduates from relevant level 4 programmes are eligible to apply for enrolment into this programme.  \n\r\nGraduates of the Bachelor of Physiotherapy (Honours) are positioned to pathway into postgraduate and doctoral programmes at Wintec or another educational institute.","developedBy":"Waikato Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3892"},"4002":{"i":"4002","entryRequirements":"Entry into the Master of Nursing Science (Pre-registration) programme is via a recognised bachelor's degree with a minimum 65% in the third year of their qualifying degree; which is considered relevant to health science or appropriate health or allied professional qualification Wintec currently offers opportunities for individuals to undertake a number of degrees that may qualify as entry points. Candidates with relevant or equivalent qualifications from other institutions may also apply to gain entry. Candidates who have not previously studied science or health science will have the opportunity to complete an online science preparation prior to commencement of the Master of Nursing Science (Pre-registration) programme. Candidates who have English as a second language are required to have an International English Language Test System (IELTS) Academic band score of 7.0 with no individual band score less than 7.0 or equivalent. The English proficiency requirements are in response to stakeholder consultation which request students undertake Clinical Practicum from Semester 1. Clinical Practicum requires students to communicate effectively in practice including responding in rapidly changing situations and emergencies. Candidates must complete their application for selection at least two months prior to the commencement of the programme. Applications received after this point will be considered on a case-by-case basis. Candidates may be required to attend an individual interview as part of the selection process.","strategicPurposeStatement":"This is a taught Master's programme. To utilise clinical judgement, evidence-based practice and clinical inquiry when working with health consumers, their  \n\r\nwhānau and inter-professional colleagues, to develop and deliver evidence based therapeutic care plans. To \n\r\ndemonstrate relational practice, cultural safety, whanaungatanga, and manaakitanga in the care provided.","graduateProfile":"Exhibit capable and resilient practice in relational and collaborative ways, to meet the Hauora needs of people, whānau and communities, underpinned by a commitment to Te Tiriti o Waitangi and Māori health. Critically evaluate conceptual, cultural, and evidence bases for nursing practice and use reflexive strategies to understand the complexity of health and illness experiences from the perspectives of individuals, whānau and community. - Demonstrate advocacy and critical action to improve Hauora for Māori and priority populations based on epidemiological patterns in population health, inequities in health, and wider societal influences. - Demonstrate highly developed communication and comprehensive assessment skills to establish differential diagnoses for the planning and coordination of person-centred care in nursing practice. - Practice effective clinical reasoning and decision-making with individuals, whānau, community and interprofessional colleagues that reflect collaboration, flexibility and leadership in complex and rapidly changing healthcare environments. - Apply professional, legal, ethical, and socio-political knowledge in nursing practice, including the impact of rapidly changing technology and expanding knowledge on sustainable, individual and whakapapa\u0002centred care. - Exhibit self-awareness, emotional intelligence, kawa whakaruruhau, cultural safety and recognition of the impact of practitioners' actions on manaakitanga and people-centred care in nursing practice. - Critically engage with rangahau or research and health policy and translate evidence into nursing practice.","educationPathway":"Graduates from relevant level degree programmes who meet the entry requirements are eligible to apply for enrolment into this programme. Graduates with a non-science degree must complete an online science preparation component prior to commencement of the programme.  \n\r\nPlease note: NCNZ is currently undertaking scoping exercises in registered nurse community prescribing preparation, education for internationally qualified nurses and a review of the registered nurse scope of practice. The outcome of these scoping exercises has the potential to lead to new and innovative ways for nurses to practice and new education and practice pathways that are currently unknown.  \n\r\nGraduates of the MNSc(Pre-reg) programme are positioned to pathway, with the potential to receive cross credit, to enter postgraduate programmes at Wintec including:  \n\r\n* Post Graduate Diploma in Nursing, as a pathway to NCNZ registered Nurse Prescriber,  \n\r\n* Master of Nursing, as a pathway to NCNZ registration in the Nurse Practitioner scope of practice or advanced nursing practice or a research dissertation, or  \n\r\nMaster of Nursing Science (Pre-registration)","developedBy":"Waikato Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=4002"},"4130":{"i":"4130","entryRequirements":"Registered health professional/counsellor, NZ practicing certificate (or equivalent), Bachelor degree (or equivalent) AND employed in relevant clinical service for minimum three days (22.5 hours) per week.   \n\r\nInternational: IELTS 6.5 (no band lower than 6), or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The purpose of this programme is to provide the health and social sector with graduates who have attained advanced knowledge and scholarship through application of research to their professional practice context in Advanced Paramedic Practice, Paramedic Community Care, Pacific Health Leadership, Palliative Care, Perioperative Nursing, Gerontology, Intellectual Disability, Forensic Practice, Primary Mental Health Care, and Talk Therapies. Each endorsement contributes to the objectives for the tertiary education and health sectors in relationship to their specific/specialty population. The endorsed programme also contributes to the New Zealand Health Strategy which aims to ensure that health workers meet the demand for services that integrate cultural practices, concepts and diverse world views into high-quality, evidence informed health services.","graduateProfile":"Graduates will be able to:     \n\n\n\r\nDemonstrate advanced professional knowledge and skills in a specialist field in which they work     \n\n\n\r\nApply leadership skills effectively in interprofessional teams within a specialised field.     \n\n\n\r\nEvaluate and integrate best practice principles in specialty practice for the provision of high-quality services to diverse people and communities      \n\n\n\r\nCritically analyse practice development trends, issues and existing solutions in relation to health and wellbeing of people, and whānau appropriate to a specialised field.","educationPathway":"Successful graduates may gain credits towards Master's studies.","developedBy":"New Zealand Institute of Skills and Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=4130"},"4159":{"i":"4159","entryRequirements":"Academic Requirements  \n\r\n- Postgraduate Diploma in a health field (120 credits at level 8). \n\n\n\r\nAlternative Requirements \n\r\n- If you do not meet the Academic entry criteria above, you may be admitted to the Postgraduate Certificate in Health Practice, and upon successful completion of two courses (B average) from the list of approved courses for the Postgraduate Certificate in Health Practice, gain admission to the Master of Health Science;  \n\r\nor \n\r\n- provide evidence of having completed a relevant professional qualification; and \n\r\n- provide evidence of successful completion of a relevant qualification or programme of study which is equivalent to those of first degree graduates, through the submission of a portfolio of evidence.  \n\n\n\r\nAdditional Requirements \n\r\nInterview \n\r\nApplicants who meet academic entry criteria may be required to attend an interview. \n\n\n\r\nEnglish Requirements \n\r\nIf English is not the applicant's first language, applicants will need to provide a result from a test or qualification on the acceptable alternatives English Proficiency Outcomes Chart.  Applicants who do not have evidence of English language skills and are a New Zealand citizen or permanent resident, may contact Ara for an assessment. \n\r\n- IELTS 6.5 Academic (no lower than 6.5 in any subtest). \n\n\n\r\nNote:   \n\r\nIELTS scores used must be taken from a single IELTS Test Report Form and are valid for two years from the date of the test. \n\r\nThe English Language requirements for this programme are higher than the minimum set by NZQA, therefore; applicants who have achieved NCEA Level 3 University Entrance may be required to provide evidence of English Language skills.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The aim of this programme is to enable students to critically evaluate, and independently apply, highly specialised knowledge and skills within their specialist area. Students will be able to show critical awareness of issues within health and be at the forefront of knowledge development within their specialist area. The Master of Health Science, option A (by course work), also enables students to demonstrate mastery of their specialised area of practice or knowledge through the completion of a piece of literary work which is highly clinically focused. The Master of Health Science, option B (by thesis), enables students on  graduation  to also be able to provide leadership through research, and contribute to ongoing development in their area of practice. The target market is health professionals who would like to advance their knowledge and skills in independent research and who may consider an advanced level of scholarship through engaging in the future in PhD level study.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Master of Health Science will be able to: \n\r\n1. analyse and apply advanced knowledge and research within their area of practice; \n\r\n2. analyse complex health issues and generate solutions; \n\r\n3. critically evaluate evidence within an interprofessional health context; \n\r\n4. demonstrate mastery of specialised knowledge within their specialist area of practice. \n\r\n5. demonstrate capacity for leadership through research and/or advanced scholarship within their specialist practice. \n\r\n6. plan, execute and complete a piece of literary work or original research thereby contributing to ongoing development in their area of practice.","educationPathway":"Graduates of these qualifications may seek enrolment in further postgraduate qualification programmes.","developedBy":"Ara Institute of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=4159"},"4278":{"i":"4278","entryRequirements":"Candidates are required to have gained: \n\r\n1. an undergraduate degree assessed as relevant by the Team Manager, or \n\r\n2. a qualification approved as equivalent by the Team Manager. \n\r\nCandidates who have not gained a relevant undergraduate degree or equivalent qualification may submit a portfolio and, if the application is successful, may be admitted on an ad eundum statem basis.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Certificate in Mental Health and Addiction provides specialised and applied mental health and addiction knowledge for people with existing bachelor degrees looking to gain entry into the mental health and addiction industry.","graduateProfile":"A graduate of the Postgraduate Certificate in Mental Health and Addiction will: \n\r\n* Articulate a professional body of knowledge in relation to mental health and addiction, its relationship to ethical codes of practice, and its location in organisational and professional contexts \n\r\n* Develop a well-integrated theoretical framework to underpin their mental health and addiction practice \n\r\n* Develop intentionality in mental health and addiction practice to facilitate in-depth critical reflection, restorative and accountable practice for practitioners in interdisciplinary environments \n\r\n* Demonstrate analytic rigour in evaluating  knowledge for expert practice within interdisciplinary environments \n\r\n* Respond to the demands and challenges of professional practice using reflexive strategies to nurture and cultivate the professional self \n\r\n* Use critical enquiry approaches to evaluate research findings for health and social service practice.","educationPathway":"The Postgraduate Certificate in Mental Health and Addiction will position graduates to move into further postgraduate study.","developedBy":"Waikato Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=4278"},"AU5633":{"i":"AU5633","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelors or bachelors honours level degree or its equivalent, with a minimum GPA. Selection criteria apply.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be eligible to apply to the NCNZ for registration. They will be clinically competent, knowledgeable and informed practitioners work-ready for employment as a Registered Nurse.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5633"},"OO0438":{"i":"OO0438","entryRequirements":"A relevant Bachelors degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The qualification is an entry level qualification for Medical technicians working in the fields of sleep medicine, and cardiology.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0438"},"CN0211":{"i":"CN0211","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand university entrance qualification, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates have a theoretical and practical understanding, and introductory clinical experience in the field of communication disorders and the knowledge to begin a clinical career assisting clients as clinicians in schools and hospital settings, or pursue further study through to doctoral level. Graduates will have gained skills to provide services to children who have difficulty communicating because of problems in language development, in learning to read, with stutters or with difficulties producing speech appropriate to their age. Graduates will have gained skills to practice in medical settings providing services to those who have lost the ability to communicate or swallow effectively due to stroke, degenerative disease, brain injury or cancer.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0211"},"ST4963":{"i":"ST4963","entryRequirements":"The normal requirement for entry is an undergraduate degree in health science (nursing/midwifery). It is expected applicants will be in current clinical practice at least 0.4 full-time equivalent position. However, applicants who are unable to meet this will be assessed by the postgraduate programme co-ordinator to ensure they have appropriate clinical placements.","strategicPurposeStatement":"To enable health professionals to develop skills of research, critical analysis, constructive synthesis and advanced practice in their discipline.","graduateProfile":"*","educationPathway":"*","developedBy":"Southern Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=ST4963"},"AU5764":{"i":"AU5764","entryRequirements":"Completed a Bachelor of Medicine and Bachelor of Surgery or equivalent with minimum GPA, have one year of work experience and hold relevant registration, or have completed the Degree of Bachelor of Nursing or Master of Nursing Science with minimum GPA, hold relevant registration and have completed or be enrolled into a Nurse Practitioner Masters degree programme, or have passed 60 points in the Postgraduate Certificate in Paediatrics or Postgraduate Diploma in Paediatrics with a minimum GPA.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MPaed graduates will be culturally competent healthcare professionals with expert knowledge and skills in the care of paediatric patients and their whanau for common clinical presentations. Graduates will be able to stabilise paediatric emergencies and work within an interdisciplinary team to provide ongoing and definitive care. Graduates will be able to critically appraise literature and local protocols in order to regularly upskill and uphold best clinical practices for themselves and the teams and organisations in which they work. They will actively participate in research to contribute and improve the quality and safety of paediatric care and equitable outcomes for local communities - including for Maori and marginalised populations.","graduateProfile":"Written assignments, critical reflections, tests/examinations, clinical portfolio and research project.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5764"},"CN1244":{"i":"CN1244","entryRequirements":"A recognised undergraduate Nursing degree, have a current Registered Nurse practicing certificate from the Nursing Council of New Zealand|Te Kaunihere Tapuhi o Aotearoa and have three years' equivalent full-time practice as a Registered Nurse in the area in which they intend to prescribe.  At least one year of practice must be in New Zealand and have access to an approved clinical placement with mentorship by a Nurse Practitioner or Medical Practitioner.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this programme will have the knowledge and skills developed through theoretical courses, scholarly inquiry, and clinical practice experience to work as a member of a collaborative team in advanced nursing practice. They will be eligible to apply to the Nursing Council of New Zealand to become a registered nurse prescriber in a designated specialty or with people with long-term conditions.","graduateProfile":"A range of assessments will be used including coursework, examination, OSCE (Objective Structured Clinical Examination), portfolio, clinical diary and case studies.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN1244"},"OO0490":{"i":"OO0490","entryRequirements":"To be considered for admission, applicants must achieve a grade point average of at least A- across all papers prescribed for the third year of the Bachelor of Physiotherapy degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this degree programme will have the knowledge, skills and attributes required for entry-level practice in the physiotherapy profession. Graduates will be able to demonstrate a high level of research-informed clinical practice, produce research outputs at a standard suitable for internationally peer-reviewed publications, and embark on postgraduate study at the doctoral level.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0490"},"CN0526":{"i":"CN0526","entryRequirements":"An approved Bachelor's degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be prepared with the public health knowledge and skills to work in a multi-cultural society, applying a critical understanding of their responsibilities to Te Tiriti. They will have applied public health knowledge to analyse data and develop and evaluate evidence-based interventions to improve population health outcomes.","graduateProfile":"A range of assessments will be used including written assignments, presentations, reflections, practical assignments, and group work.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0526"},"WI0974":{"i":"WI0974","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand bachelor degree with honours or master's degree, with at least second class honours (first division) or distinction. Applicants must have qualified for the award of a recognised health professional qualification and must produce evidence of at least three years of service as a health professional.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will:   * Provide clinical leadership in a range of clinical settings across the continuum of care and the lifespan;    * Generate, critique and utilise nursing knowledge, and contribute to the evidence based of practice through research,   * Practise in joint clinical and academic roles that integrate practice based and theoretical knowledge, and   * Provide culturally responsive care and support to people to manage their health and wellbeing.     Graduates of the University of Waikato Nursing postgraduate programmes will provide leadership to the nursing workforce and health services, articulate models of care to address population health needs, produce research that extends the boundaries of nursing knowledge, inform health policy with knowledge derived from critically examined clinical experience and advocate for strategies that address inequities in health care regionally and nationally.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0974"},"AU5068":{"i":"AU5068","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelor's degree or equivalent and at least 2 years' relevant work experience","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGDipPH graduates will understand the principles of public health, the measurement and monitoring of health status and actions required to promote and protect public health.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5068"},"OO0518":{"i":"OO0518","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree in medical imaging or an acceptable equivalent qualification, and evidence of ability for advanced level academic study.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have the capacity to assimilate information at an advanced level in the field of medical imaging.","graduateProfile":"NA","educationPathway":"NA","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0518"},"OO0429":{"i":"OO0429","entryRequirements":"Candidates intending to complete the MDentTech by papers and a thesis must have a Bachelor of Dental Technology degree or equivalent. Candidates intending to complete by thesis only must have a Postgraduate Diploma in Dental Technology or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The programme will provide a learning framework that will allow candidates to advance their research and academic knowledge and technical skills in aspects of dental technology and dental biomaterials. The Thesis for the Master of Dental Technology is focused on research in the area of advanced biomaterials and dental technology. The programmes goal is to provide dental technicians with advanced skills in a range of disciplines that will be of benefit to the dental profession and the public, and to provide an academic and / or research career pathway for dental technicians. The programme aims to broaden students knowledge and skills in advanced dental technology and biomaterials and update them on current advances in practice and issues involving the delivery of dental technology to general dentists and specialists. Students will be able to critically evaluate these concepts, will understand scientific method and be able to conduct research. The thesis will enable the candidate to carry out independent research on a specific question.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0429"},"VI003S":{"i":"VI003S","entryRequirements":"To be admitted to the programme students need to hold a Masters or Postgraduate Diploma with a minimum GPA of B, have at least five years' professional experience and have established to the satisfaction of the Associate Dean that they are capable of proceeding with the doctorate.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Doctor of Nursing is designed for established professionals in the health sector who wish to enhance their research-related professional practice and management. Graduates will be able to engage in high quality independent research and inquiry into their own practice and contribute original knowledge to improving health related practice, systems and policy. They will be able to link, in a coherent and rigorous manner, theory and research to questions of professional practice and management of the health system. Graduates will have advanced knowledge of their professional field and be able to evaluate and apply research and scholarly literature. They will adopt an investigative, open-minded, critical and reflective stance in addressing scholarly and professional problems from different perspectives, skillfully communicate research results to both academic and professional communities, and be able to engage in and critique the process of peer review. Graduates will demonstrate leadership in the areas of their professional endeavor as well as high personal ethical standards and behaviours in scholarly and professional contexts, and respect and maintain intellectual integrity.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI003S"},"OO0476":{"i":"OO0476","entryRequirements":"An average grade of at least B+ in the final year of the BDentTech programme.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Bachelor of Dental Technology with Honours (BDentTech(Hons)) graduates will have research experience, and academic and practical knowledge in the areas of dental technology and dental biomaterials. The programme aims to broaden students knowledge, over and above that obtained through the ordinary Bachelor of Dental Technology (BDentTech) programme, and to enable them to critically evaluate concepts, understand scientific methods, and be skilled at conducting pertinent research. They will have excellent communication skills, enabling them to communicate with colleagues from an informed perspective. Graduates will be positioned to embark on an advanced professional career or further academic study at Masters or PhD level.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0476"},"OO0255":{"i":"OO0255","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree or other three-year health professional qualification; plus appropriate experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"This certificate programme enables health professionals to specialise in areas of practice at postgraduate level.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0255"},"VI003O":{"i":"VI003O","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will demonstrate advanced knowledge in one of seven health subject areas: health leadership and management; health policy, planning and service delivery; health promotion; midwifery; nursing; professional practice; workplace health and safety. They will be able to apply critical thinking to achieve new insights in their field of health, apply and communication research knowledge in their field and take a leadership role in that field.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI003O"},"AU5064":{"i":"AU5064","entryRequirements":"A medical degree and current registration as a medical practitioner with access to clinical work.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGCertMedSc graduates will be skilled practitioners in a specialised field of medical science.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5064"},"OO0414":{"i":"OO0414","entryRequirements":"2 year programme in Dental Therapy and 2 years appropriate experience","strategicPurposeStatement":"This postgraduate diploma provides practising dental therapists with advanced knowledge and training in improving oral health.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0414"},"OO0058":{"i":"OO0058","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor of Dental Surgery degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"This degree involves supervised research and clinical practice in a chosen area. Graduates have advanced knowledge in the field, the ability to study independently, and to conduct original research to internationally recognised standards.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0058"},"OO0411":{"i":"OO0411","entryRequirements":"The degrees of Bachelor of Medicine and Bachelor of Surgery, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Holders of this certificate are accredited as aviation medical examiners in accordance with the training requirements of the International Civil Aviation Organisation (ICAO) and most civil aviation licensing authorities around the world.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0411"},"AU5130":{"i":"AU5130","entryRequirements":"Medical degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGDipObstMedGyn graduates will have the knowledge and skills to improve the reproductive health of all women and the welfare of their babies in their registered medical professional role.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5130"},"OT4898":{"i":"OT4898","entryRequirements":"Occupational therapists entering this programme must hold a Bachelor of Occupational Therapy  degree or equivalent. Applicants holding an equivalent qualification must be from a World Federation of Occupational Therapists (WFOT) approved programme.\n\n\n\r\nInternational applicants for whom English is not a first language are required to have an IELTS overall band score (Academic) of 6.5 with a minimum score of 6.5 in each band. These IELTS scores align with what is required in to apply for registration as an occupational therapist in Aotearoa New Zealand. Applicants who do not meet all the academic requirements for entry into the programme can make an application to the Head of School, who will consider the application on a case-by-case basis. Entry to the programme will be at the Head of School's discretion. \n\n\n\r\nSelection Criteria* \n\r\nĀkonga who meet the entry criteria will be accepted on a first come, first served basis until all places are full. After the programme is full, applicants who meet the entry criteria will then be placed on a waiting list and informed if a place becomes available.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The aim of the Postgraduate Certificate in Occupational Therapy Practice is to produce occupational therapists with highly developed professional reasoning skills who can lead advancements in occupational therapy practice within their team and/or profession. They will be able to critically analyse advanced theoretical and /or specialised knowledge in relation to occupational therapy practice. Utilising current research, they will be expert in the application of evidence informed- practice and contribute to improved outcomes for the people they work with.","graduateProfile":"By the end of this programme, graduates will be able to:  \n\r\n- Critically evaluate relevant literature, to improve the effectiveness of occupational therapy interventions in Aotearoa New Zealand's bicultural context  \n\r\n- Critically review research to support their own and others' practice developments  \n\r\n- Critically analyse practice problems from different perspectives  \n\r\n- Generate solutions to complex practice problems  \n\r\n- Demonstrate evidence of advanced knowledge in a specialist field or professional practice.","educationPathway":"Graduates will be able to progress to further postgraduate study.","developedBy":"Otago Polytechnic","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OT4898"},"VI003P":{"i":"VI003P","entryRequirements":"Entry to the Postgraduate Certificate in Health requires a Bachelor of Health or a Bachelor's degree in a relevant discipline.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will demonstrate advanced knowledge in one of seven health subject areas: health leadership and management; health policy, planning and service delivery; health promotion; midwifery; nursing; professional practice; workplace health and safety. They will be able to apply critical thinking to achieve new insights in their field of health, apply and communication research knowledge in their field and take a leadership role in that field.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI003P"},"WI0984":{"i":"WI0984","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand Bachelors degree or equivalent, completed at a specified minimum level of attainment.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will:  * Demonstrate the competencies of a Registered Nurse as determined by the Nursing Council of New Zealand;  * Show developing skills in clinical leadership;  * Generate, critique and utilise nursing knowledge, and contribute to the evidence base of practice through research;  * Be able to integrate practice based and theoretical knowledge; and  * Provide culturally responsive care and support to people to manage their health and wellbeing.  Graduates of the Whare Wananga o Waikato - University of Waikato MNursPrac programme will demonstrate clinical competencies required by the Nursing Council of New Zealand for practice as a Registered Nurse. They will be prepared to provide leadership to the nursing workforce and health services, articulate models of care to address population health needs, produce research that extends the boundaries of nursing knowledge, inform health policy with knowledge derived from critically examined clinical experience and advocate for strategies that address inequities in health care regionally and nationally.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0984"},"OO0445":{"i":"OO0445","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor of Dental Surgery or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Through supervised research and clinical practice graduates will be able to practise as specialist dental practitioners. Graduates will develop critical assessment skills in evaluating research and its relevance to contemporary clinical dental practice.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0445"},"AU4017":{"i":"AU4017","entryRequirements":"Completed a Bachelor of Medicine and Bachelor of Surgery or an approved equivalent medical qualification and have the research experience, ability, and disciplinary training to undertake doctoral level research.","strategicPurposeStatement":"An MD graduate will demonstrate advanced skills in the definition, management and communication of original research in a specialist area and a high level of potential for independence, creativity, innovation and leadership throughout their career.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU4017"},"OO0404":{"i":"OO0404","entryRequirements":"Degree or appropriate alternative qualification","strategicPurposeStatement":"This postgraduate certificate provides a nationally recognised qualification for Health Professionals engaged in the delivery of primary health care.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0404"},"OO0229":{"i":"OO0229","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree or other three-year health professional qualification.","strategicPurposeStatement":"This degree programme involves in-depth study, training and supervised research in health science subjects.  Graduates have advanced knowledge in their chosen field, and are able to study independently and carry out original research.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0229"},"OO0517":{"i":"OO0517","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree in medical imaging or an acceptable equivalent qualification, and evidence of ability for advanced level academic study.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have the capacity to assimilate information at an advanced level in the field of medical imaging.","graduateProfile":"NA","educationPathway":"NA","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0517"},"VI00E5":{"i":"VI00E5","entryRequirements":"Bachelor's degree and 3 years nursing experience  REPLACED by VI00N4 (PGCert in Clinical Nursing)","strategicPurposeStatement":"To provide professional development programmes in   specialised areas of nursing  REPLACED by VI00N4 (PGCert in Clinical Nursing)","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00E5"},"CN0996":{"i":"CN0996","entryRequirements":"An approved Bachelor's degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Students will have developed their knowledge and skills in the area of sport science to master's level and be able to reflect each of the graduate attributes. They will be able to conduct research in academic of commercial contest and have the skills necessary to work successfully in an applied context. They will be able to seek employment in an Aotearoa New Zealand context with bicultural competence and confidence.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0996"},"VI00X6":{"i":"VI00X6","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree and New Zealand Registered Nurse status.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will demonstrate advanced knowledge in their specialist area of nursing practice. They will employ knowledge of pathophysiological concepts to their practice, to their understanding of current nursing practice issues and to their assessment skills. The diploma may lead to more advanced study such as a Master of Nursing Science degree. Employment pathways include advanced clinical or management nursing roles.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00X6"},"AK3830":{"i":"AK3830","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelor's degree must be completed with a B grade average or higher in papers at level 7.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MNSc graduates will be eligible to apply for registration with the Nursing Council of New Zealand and will have beginning practitioner knowledge, skills and understanding of nursing. They will demonstrate leadership in the integration of nursing into healthcare services within a complex environment. They will be critical and reflective, with strong applied research capability. They will demonstrate the ability to engage in research and may progress to further postgraduate advanced nursing practice study, or academic study at the doctoral level.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK3830"},"AU5741":{"i":"AU5741","entryRequirements":"Completed the requirements for a Bachelors degree in a relevant subject with a minimum GPA.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGDipStrokeCare graduates will know, understand, apply and communicate the principles, evidence, and practices that constitute evidence-based stroke care at every stage of the patient journey. They will be prepared to work as culturally safe, reflective practitioners, able to function within an interprofessional team and contribute to improvements in the quality and safety of stroke care.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5741"},"OO0428":{"i":"OO0428","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand medical degree, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be able to attain general competencies in aviation medicine. They will have studied specific aspects of aviation medicine practice, primarily in occupational medicine, aviation human factors, or in aeromedical evacuation.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0428"},"CN0944":{"i":"CN0944","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor's degree of relevance to the health sciences or an equivalent appropriate health or allied professional qualification.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have gained an advanced introduction to research, knowledge of a range of aspects of the New Zealand health system and issues in the health sector. They will have the ability to understand and think critically about a limited range of health-related areas.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0944"},"OO0430":{"i":"OO0430","entryRequirements":"no change","strategicPurposeStatement":"Persons with this diploma will have acquired current knowledge in dental, applied biomaterials science and advanced dental technology skills. They will be committed to the highest academic and technical standards, and to lifelong learning and continuing professional development. Students will be able to critically evaluate scientific methodology and be able to provide advanced prosthetic technical support to specialist dentists such as prosthodontists and oral and maxillofacial surgeons. The programme ensures that candidates will be able to apply their course work to the New Zealand Dental Technicians Board and Health Practitioners Competency Assurance Act (2003) accreditation / continuing professional development requirements.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0430"},"AU5504":{"i":"AU5504","entryRequirements":"Completion of the first three years of a MBChB degree from The University of Auckland, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The programme gives well-performing medical students the opportunity to gain research training before continuing with their medical education. Graduates will develop increased skills in critical reasoning and knowledge of research and research methodology.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5504"},"VI00W7":{"i":"VI00W7","entryRequirements":"Relevant degree in health, medicine, neuroscience and psychology, biomedical science, or biostatistics to an appropriate level.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Provision of a comprehensive understanding and skill base to enable existing and future clinical researchers to undertake clinical research at a postgraduate level.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00W7"},"OO0060":{"i":"OO0060","entryRequirements":"A candidate must normally be a graduate of the University of Otago, with a Bachelor of Dental Surgery degree conferred at least five years before candidature.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have demonstrated special excellence in a field of relevance to dentistry.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0060"},"OO0212":{"i":"OO0212","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor of Physiotherapy degree or equivalent; registration with the New Zealand Physiotherapy Board; and the equivalent of at least two years' full-time relevant clinical experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have advanced knowledge in a designated area of physiotherapy, and the ability to study independently and carry out original research.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0212"},"OO0241":{"i":"OO0241","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor of Medical Laboratory Science degree or equivalent","strategicPurposeStatement":"This course is for well-qualified Bachelor of Medical Laboratory Science graduates, and other medical laboratory scientists who have an aptitude for research. It is designed as preparation for full-time research for the Master of Medical Laboratory Science.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0241"},"AK3662":{"i":"AK3662","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelor's degree completed to a merit standard.","strategicPurposeStatement":"BHSc(Hons) graduates will have in-depth knowledge, in their chosen field of health science. They will have the research and critical thinking skills for further postgraduate study at master?s or doctoral level or for their own sphere of practice.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK3662"},"VI003Q":{"i":"VI003Q","entryRequirements":"To be admitted to the programme students need to hold a Masters or Postgraduate Diploma with a minimum GPA of B, have at least five years' professional experience and have established to the satisfaction of the Associate Dean that they are capable of proceeding with the doctorate.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Doctor of Health is designed for established professionals in the health sector who wish to enhance their research-related professional practice and management. Graduates will be able to engage in high quality independent research and inquiry into their own practice and contribute original knowledge to improving health related practice, systems and policy. They will be able to link, in a coherent and rigorous manner, theory and research to questions of professional practice and management of the health system. Graduates will have advanced knowledge of their professional field and be able to evaluate and apply research and scholarly literature. They will adopt an investigative, open-minded, critical and reflective stance in addressing scholarly and professional problems from different perspectives, skillfully communicate research results to both academic and professional communities, and be able to engage in and critique the process of peer review. Graduates will demonstrate leadership in the areas of their professional endeavor as well as high personal ethical standards and behaviours in scholarly and professional contexts, and respect and maintain intellectual integrity.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI003Q"},"HBH002":{"i":"HBH002","entryRequirements":"1.  An undergraduate degree in a health science with a B pass or better.  A minimum of two years clinical practice may be an advantage.\n\r\n2. Where the applicant may have less than a B+ average in her/his undergraduate degree s/he may be provisionally accepted.\n\r\n3.  Where an applicant does not hold an undergraduate degree in health science:\n\r\n- the applicant shall provide evidence of having completed a relevant professional qualification, and\n\r\n- provide evidence of successful completion of a relevant qualification or programme of study which is equivalent to those of first degree graduates, through the submission of a portfolio of evidence.\n\r\n4. A personal interview may assist the application process.\n\r\nApproved subjects include Health Science.\n\r\nApplicants must be Registered Health Professionals including social Workers, who hold a current Annual Practising Certificate.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have developed specialty practice competencies to enter  specialty areas of mental health nursing and be introduced to the concept and competencies of advanced practice.","graduateProfile":"The Postgraduate Certificate in Health Science offers a selection of\n\r\ncourses designed to meet the needs of health practitioners, health\n\r\nsector managers and other professionals whose practice has a focus\n\r\non health. The Postgraduate Certificate in Health Science may\n\r\nbe completed with or without a specialty option. For Registered Nurses with a current New Zealand annual practicing certificate, application can be made with the Nursing Council of New Zealand for an endorsement in practice","educationPathway":"Pending successful completion of the required academic entry\n\r\nrequirements, graduates of the Postgraduate Certificate in Health\n\r\nScience may progress to the Postgraduate Diploma in Health Science, or\n\r\nMaster of Health Science. Registered Nurse graduates may progress to\n\r\nthe Master of Nursing.","developedBy":"Eastern Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Quality Assurance Division, NZQA","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=HBH002"},"MY1013":{"i":"MY1013","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Speech and Language Therapy and a Postgraduate Certificate in Speech and Language Therapy, or a Bachelor of Speech and Language Therapy (Honours); or equivalent. One year of clinical experience; selection.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be able to extend knowledge through intellectual independence, analytic rigour and critical evaluation. They will be able to master theoretical issues and research methods, critically analyse and apply knowledge; understand research methods and prepare research proposals, critically read and appraise research. They will know theories of communication and related disorders; and know methodological and theoretical issues that relate to cultural and linguistic diversity.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY1013"},"CN0216":{"i":"CN0216","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor's degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be well-prepared to perform the role of a speech language pathologist and will meet the standards of practice of an entry-level speech language pathologist of the New Zealand Speech-Language Therapists' Association. They will be able to understand, evaluate and critically appraise new or complex information, including findings and discussions in the literature, research analyse, evaluate and argue from evidence and work collaboratively on tasks and show leadership. They will be able to communicate concepts, results and conclusions related to research findings and design and undertake clinical practice.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0216"},"OT4806":{"i":"OT4806","entryRequirements":"Minimum academic entry criteria are: \n\r\nĀkonga are admitted to this programme after completion of the third year of an undergraduate Bachelor of Occupational Therapy degree. They are required to commence study in the Honours programme within three years of completing their degree. To be admitted to the programme ākonga must have passed all courses in the Bachelor of Occupational Therapy programme (on their first attempt). In years two and three ākonga must have achieved a minimum B grade average or equivalent. Only graded components contribute to this calculation. For courses which do not award grades ākonga must pass each course on their first attempt. Special circumstances can be considered on application by ākonga to the Head of School. \n\n\n\r\nInternational applicants for whom English is not a first language are required to have an IELTS overall band score (Academic) of 6.5 with a minimum score of 6.5 in each band. These IELTS scores align with what is required in to apply for registration as an occupational therapist in Aotearoa New Zealand. \n\n\n\r\nApplicants who do not meet all of the academic requirements for entry into the programme can make an application to the Head of School. Entry to the programme will be at the Head of School's discretion. \n\n\n\r\nOtago Polytechnic's policy AP0520.07 English Language Requirements for International Learners and those for whom English is an Additional Language Selection Criteria* \n\n\n\r\nĀkonga who meet the entry criteria will be accepted on a first come, first served basis, until all places are full. After the programme is full, applicants who meet the entry criteria will then be placed on a waiting list and informed if a place becomes available.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The aim of the Bachelor of Occupational Therapy (Honours) is to prepare graduates of the Bachelor of Occupational Therapy or equivalent to undertake research as part of their occupational therapy practice in bicultural Aotearoa New Zealand, and to pursue advanced study. The qualification will increase their knowledge in a specific area of practice and may therefore increase the range of roles into which a graduate may be employed.","graduateProfile":"By the end of this programme, graduates will be able to:  \n\r\n- Critically analyse new knowledge and ideas from a sound and rigorous theoretical basis, demonstrating intellectual independence and analytical rigour, to support further development of the occupational therapy role in traditional, emergent and/or innovative areas.  \n\r\n- Plan and conduct research, analyse results, and present findings to contribute to the ongoing development of occupational therapy theory and practice in bicultural Aotearoa New Zealand, to the satisfaction of subject experts.  \n\r\n- Critically review and further refine their knowledge understandings of Te Tiriti o Waitangi, their responsibilities to connect with and work collaboratively with Māori, and the application of this to their practice and research as occupational therapists.","educationPathway":"Graduates of this degree may pathway into further postgraduate or doctoral study.","developedBy":"Otago Polytechnic","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OT4806"},"OO0252":{"i":"OO0252","entryRequirements":"Registration for Medical Practice","strategicPurposeStatement":"This certificate provides advanced study in this discipline which deals with patients who have musculoskeletal and neural dysfunction of both an acute and chronic nature.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0252"},"OO0201":{"i":"OO0201","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Medicine and Bachelor of Surgery degrees and appropriate professional qualification","strategicPurposeStatement":"This postgraduate diploma provides aviation medicine training to registered medical practitioners.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0201"},"WK2487":{"i":"WK2487","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor of Sport and Exercise Science with a minimum B grade (65%) in the third year; or A corresponding NZ Bachelor degree with a minimum B grade (65%) in the third year; or A Postgraduate Diploma in Sport and Exercise Science with a minimum B grade average; or A corresponding NZ Postgraduate Diploma with a minimum B grade average; or Equivalent. Candidates who have English as a second language are required to have an International English Language Test System (IELTS) score of 6.5 with no individual band score lower than 6.0; or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be leading Human Performance Science practitioners, capable of working interprofessionally to deliver research-based solutions that strengthen communities in New Zealand and Internationally. The Master of Science (Human Performance Science) is designed for those who wish to extend their undergraduate degree with highly specialised knowledge in sport and exercise science, clinical exercise physiology, rehabilitation and movement related professions. It is most suited to those who wish to continue to a doctoral programme or into higher level positions in the workforce.","graduateProfile":"A graduate of the MScHP will: * Exhibit mastery of their specialist area and extended knowledge in a subject area of Human Performance Science. * Evaluate critically the findings and discussions in the literature. * Exhibit significant independent research capability and translate findings in to practice. * Demonstrate technical competence and the ability to manage ambiguity and complexity autonomously in a Human Performance setting. * Demonstrate advanced knowledge and skills in conceptual and critical thinking, reflection, problem solving and communication.","educationPathway":"Graduates from relevant level degree programmes are eligible to apply for enrolment into this programme.  \n\r\nGraduates of the Master of Science (Human Performance Science) are positioned to pathway into programmes such as a PhD in associated areas (clinical, environmental or exercise physiology; rehabilitation; sports nutrition; sports psychology; strength and conditioning; youth athlete development) or a further Masters degree in an associated specialty (e.g. dietetics).","developedBy":"Waikato Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WK2487"},"VI005S":{"i":"VI005S","entryRequirements":"Entry to the PGDipPAH requires a bachelor's degree in a relevant discipline or significant practical, professional, or cultural experience as determined by the Associate Dean (Students) with a B average.  These requirements can be waived by the Associate Dean (Students) for a candidate who has had extensive practical, professional or cultural experience of an appropriate level.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Diploma of Physical Activity and Hauora will have advanced skills to lead change amongst health promotion colleagues and communities. They will be critical thinkers that bring innovation and social justice to policy and community development. Graduates will have advanced skills in applying evidence-based practice and matauranga Maori as well as evaluating, explaining, and improving health promotion knowledge in the physical activity sector of Aotearoa New Zealand and internationally.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI005S"},"OO0425":{"i":"OO0425","entryRequirements":"Postgraduate Diploma in Travel Medicine, or equivalent; completion of research methods papers relevant to health sciences to the value of 30 credits.","strategicPurposeStatement":"This programme is a comprehensive course of study for health professionals working in the field of travel and migrant medicine. Graduates will have a thorough and rigorous understanding of the discipline of travel medicine, including tropical and migrant medicine; a broad knowledge of health care systems and the place of travel medicine within those systems, particularly in relation to effective delivery in primary health care settings; the ability to contribute significantly to new interdisciplinary developments in health care delivery; the ability to contribute significantly to an increasing international body of knowledge in travel medicine; the ability to utilise the principles of evidence-based practice and incorporate these into the safe and effective practice and delivery of travel medicine; and an understanding of research methodology appropriate to the discipline, including both quantitative and qualitative methods.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0425"},"PR4801":{"i":"PR4801","entryRequirements":"Registered nurse with current NZ practicing certificate (or equivalent), Bachelor degree (or equivalent) AND relevant clinical employment for a minimum of 2 days (15 hours) per week. \n\r\n(International: IELTS 7.0 in each band)","strategicPurposeStatement":"The purpose of this programme is to provide the health and social sector with graduates who have attained advanced knowledge and scholarship through application of research to their professional practice context.\n\r\nGraduates will have gained additional, knowledge and skills to provide specialty Registered Nurse care for a variety of primary health care settings including Well Child/Tamariki Ora (Plunket nursing), district nursing, public health nursing, practice nursing, aged and residential care setting, Whanau ora, occupational health, youth health.","graduateProfile":"Graduates will have the ability to work effectively in interprofessional teams and have enhanced skills for the provision of high quality services to diverse people and communities.  Graduates will also have advanced knowledge about the specialist field of primary health care nursing practice.","educationPathway":"Successful graduates may gain credits towards Master's studies.","developedBy":"New Zealand Institute of Skills and Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Quality Assurance Division, NZQA","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=PR4801"},"WI0978":{"i":"WI0978","entryRequirements":"Bachelors degree or equivalent, completed at a specified minimum level of attainment.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will:  * Provide clinical leadership in a range of clinical settings across the continuum of care and the lifespan;  * Generate, critique and utilise nursing knowledge, and contribute to the evidence based of practice through research;  * Realise in clinical practice and professional leadership, commitments to Te Tiriti o Waitangi as the founding document for health in Aotearoa-NZ;   * Practise in joint clinical and academic roles that integrate practice based and theoretical knowledge, and  * Provide culturally responsive care and support to people to manage their health and wellbeing.    Graduates of University of Waikato Nursing postgraduate programmes will provide leadership to the nursing workforce and health services, articulate models of care to address population health needs, produce research that extends the boundaries of nursing knowledge, inform health policy with knowledge derived from critically examined clinical experience and advocate for strategies that address inequities in health care regionally and nationally.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0978"},"VI005T":{"i":"VI005T","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Certificate of Physical Activity and Hauora will have advanced skills to lead change amongst health promotion colleagues and communities. They will be critical thinkers that bring innovation and social justice to policy and community development. Graduates will have advanced skills in applying evidence-based practice and matauranga Maori as well as evaluating, explaining, and improving health promotion knowledge in the physical activity sector of Aotearoa New Zealand and internationally.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI005T"},"AU5675":{"i":"AU5675","entryRequirements":"Completed Parts I, II, and III of the Degree of Bachelor of Pharmacy with a minimum Grade Point Average. An interview may be required.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the BPharm(Hons) will be eligible to seek internship pharmacy registration with the Evolve programme administered on behalf of the New Zealand Pharmacy Council and to be employed to provide intern pharmacy services within hospital, community and other pharmacies in New Zealand. Graduates of the BPharm(Hons) programme will be critical, reflective practitioners with advanced inquiry and applied research capabilities, able to pursue personal professional goals and further pharmacy postgraduate research.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5675"},"WI1014":{"i":"WI1014","entryRequirements":"Bachelors degree in a relevant subject with at least a B grade average across the 300 level papers or equivalent, and by selection process to ensure admission criteria is met by the University, and for registration to the Pharmacy Council of New Zealand.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the Master of Pharmacy Practice will be eligible to apply for registration as an Intern Pharmacist with the Pharmacy Council of New Zealand, Te Pou Whakamana Kaimatu o Aotearoa. Upon completion of an approved Intern Training Programme and achieving a pass in the Pharmacy Council Assessment Centre, graduates will be eligible to apply for registration as a Pharmacist. Graduates will be well prepared for further postgraduate studies in pharmacy and other related areas. For clarity, they will need to complete a subsequent research Master's degree before progressing to doctoral study.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI1014"},"AK3558":{"i":"AK3558","entryRequirements":"An applicant must have completed a Bachelor of Health Science (Nursing) or relevant professional practice or experience in a related health field equivalent to a bachelor's degree. Evidence of current professional practice is required.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PgDipRNPres graduates will have advanced knowledge and skills in their field of practice essential for them to be able to pursue personal and professional goals, and further postgraduate study. The emphasis placed on integrating theory and practice will enhance their problem solving and analytical skills. Graduates will have advanced knowledge within a specialist field. They will have developed skills in critical thinking, problem solving and communication and be prepared for further postgraduate study. In addition, PgDipRNPres graduates will meet the preparatory education requirements for registered nurse medicine prescriptive authority.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK3558"},"AK3557":{"i":"AK3557","entryRequirements":"A relevant Bachelors degree, or relevant professional practice or experience in nursing equivalent to a professional qualification.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PgCertAdvNursPrac graduates will demonstrate an advanced level of understanding of nursing practice and will be competent and reflective practitioners. They will have well-developed skills in critical thinking, problem solving, and communication and be prepared for further postgraduate study.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK3557"},"AK3664":{"i":"AK3664","entryRequirements":"A master's degree with first or second-class honours or bachelor's degree with first or second-class honours (first division), plus a minimum of 5 years' professional experience in the field relevant to the proposed thesis topic.","strategicPurposeStatement":"DHSc graduates will have extended their practice, scholarly thinking and knowledge and will have made an original contribution to professional knowledge and practice in their area of health expertise.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK3664"},"AU0388":{"i":"AU0388","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Nursing or an approved equivalent degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"BNurs(Hons) graduates will have the knowledge and skills to practise nursing and develop scholarship and leadership in nursing. They will be critical and reflective practitioners able to pursue professional practice and further research.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU0388"},"AU5760":{"i":"AU5760","entryRequirements":"Completed a Bachelor of Medicine and Bachelor of Surgery or equivalent, have one year of work experience and hold relevant registration, or have completed the Degree of Bachelor of Nursing or Master of Nursing Science, hold relevant registration and have completed or be enrolled into a Nurse Practitioner Masters degree programme","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGCertPaed graduates will be culturally competent healthcare professionals with expert knowledge and skills in the care of paediatric patients and their whanau for common clinical presentations. Graduates will be able to identify gaps between best practice and current practice, practice according to current best practice guidelines. Graduates will develop an understanding of the underlying factors that influence inequitable patient experiences and clinical outcomes for the paediatric population.","graduateProfile":"Written assignments, critical reflections, tests/examinations, clinical portfolio and research project.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5760"},"VI00X7":{"i":"VI00X7","entryRequirements":"A bachelors degree and New Zealand Registered Nurse status.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have research skills and will apply their advanced understanding of pathophysiology to their particular practice setting. They will use their expertise to improve health outcomes in their specialist area of nursing practice and will be able to advance their career in that area. Graduates can progress to further study in the Postgraduate Diploma in Nursing Science and then to the Master of Nursing Science.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00X7"},"OO0246":{"i":"OO0246","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree or other three-year health professional qualification; plus appropriate experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Students who complete this diploma programme will have received practical training and an introduction to research in designated areas of health sciences.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0246"},"AU5762":{"i":"AU5762","entryRequirements":"Completed a Bachelor of Medicine and Bachelor of Surgery or equivalent, have one year of work experience and hold relevant registration, or have completed the Degree of Bachelor of Nursing or Master of Nursing Science, hold relevant registration and have completed or be enrolled into a Nurse Practitioner Masters degree programme, or have passed 60 points in the Postgraduate Certificate in Paediatrics.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGDipPaed graduates will be culturally competent healthcare professionals with expert knowledge and skills in the care of paediatric patients and their whanau for common clinical presentations. Graduates will be able to stabilise paediatric emergencies and work within an interdisciplinary team to provide ongoing and definitive care. Graduates will be able to critically appraise literature and local protocols in order to regularly upskill and uphold best clinical practices for themselves and the teams and organisations in which they work. They will contribute to improvements in the quality and safety of paediatric care and equitable outcomes for local communities - including for Maori and marginalised populations.","graduateProfile":"Written assignments, critical reflections, tests/examinations, clinical portfolio and research project.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5762"},"AU5792":{"i":"AU5792","entryRequirements":"A relevant Bachelors degree with a minimum Grade Point Average (GPA).","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Master of Nutrition and Dietetics is designed to prepare a student for registration as a Dietitian in New Zealand and to provide safe, competent and responsible dietetic care in a variety of health settings.?","graduateProfile":"Assessments include individual and group coursework, exams, research work.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5792"},"OO0059":{"i":"OO0059","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Dentistry degree and previous training or experience","strategicPurposeStatement":"This degree involves supervised research and advanced study. Graduates have detailed knowledge of the field, the ability to study independently, and to conduct original research to internationally recognised standards.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0059"},"OO0515":{"i":"OO0515","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this degree programme will be independent and skilled in the provision of nursing care that is reflective and integrates research, theory and practice and meets the Competencies for Registration NCNZ (2012). They will demonstrate leadership and evaluation skills with an ability to envision future development of nursing care that is responsive to New Zealand population health needs.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0515"},"AK4662":{"i":"AK4662","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand university entrance qualification or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The purpose of the proposal is to introduce a 4-year Bachelor with Honours degree in Physiotherapy, alongside the current 4-year undergraduate BHSc (Physiotherapy) AK3313 programme.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK4662"},"AK3487":{"i":"AK3487","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelor's degree or equivalent plus professional experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PgDipHSc graduates will have advanced knowledge and skills in their field of practice essential for them to be able to pursue personal professional goals and further postgraduate study. The emphasis placed on integrating theory and practice will enhance their problem solving and analytical skills.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK3487"},"OO0510":{"i":"OO0510","entryRequirements":"Applicants must normally have completed a Bachelor of Dental Surgery degree with an average grade of at least B+ in the final two years of the degree, or equivalent, and at least three years of relevant clinical experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this degree programme will be able to demonstrate advanced clinical and research skills in the area of aesthetic dentistry or rural oral health care.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0510"},"AK1015":{"i":"AK1015","strategicPurposeStatement":"To meet the needs of professionals from a range of different disciplines and occupational groups in relation to emergency management. Develop emergency management capabilities across a range of disciplines in hazard identification, risk reduction, planning, response delivery and/or co-ordination, and community recovery.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1015"},"MY1056":{"i":"MY1056","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Health Science with a major in either environmental health or environmental risk management, or equivalent. Plus a guarantee from a sponsor to provide work experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGCertEHPr graduates will have advanced knowledge to enhance professional development and skills in the area of environmental health. They will be critical thinkers, able to communicate effectively and have good quantitative skills. They will be able to solve a range of both theoretical and practical problems and have acquired the ability to work independently and with groups.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY1056"},"AU5143":{"i":"AU5143","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand university entrance qualification or an approved alternative. Must meet entry requirements of each component degree. Selection criteria apply.","strategicPurposeStatement":"BHSc/LLB(Hons) graduates will demonstrate knowledge and understanding of the content and application of elements of both Health Sciences and Law disciplines with additional enhanced research and writing skills within the law component.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5143"},"AU5740":{"i":"AU5740","entryRequirements":"Completed the requirements for a Bachelors degree in a relevant subject with a minimum GPA, or completed the requirements for a Bachelors degree in a relevant subject and passed 60 points towards the Postgraduate Certificate in Stroke Care with a minimum GPA.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MStrokeCare graduates will know, understand, apply and communicate the principles, evidence, and practices that constitute evidence-based stroke care at every stage of the patient journey. They will be prepared to work as culturally safe, reflective practitioners, able to function within an interprofessional team and contribute to improvements in the quality and safety of stroke care. Graduates will demonstrate the ability to plan and participate in clinical research and pursue further postgraduate studies.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5740"},"VI00Y8":{"i":"VI00Y8","entryRequirements":"A PGDipClinRes or other acceptable qualification and/or experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the MClinRes will lead research initiatives in clinical research.They will have substantial understanding of the research literature in a specific area of clinical research and the sophisticated experimental techniques and technologies required to undertake and analyse their research findings.They will understand the requirements of interdisciplinary research within a team, communicating their research findings across a range of forms and contexts, including the research literature and working ethically and where appropriate inclusively across cultures.Graduates will enhance the important links between University research and clinical training, improving the quality of the outputs from both sectors.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00Y8"},"OO0203":{"i":"OO0203","entryRequirements":"Postgraduate Diploma in Public Health or equivalent qualification","strategicPurposeStatement":"This degree provides in-depth study and supervised research in a chosen aspect of public health. It provides advanced knowledge in the field and the ability to study independently and carry out original research.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0203"},"AU5119":{"i":"AU5119","entryRequirements":"Completed the requirements for a Bachelors degree in a relevant subject area(s) with a minimum Grade Point Average (GPA) An interview, submission of a supplementary information form and confidential letters of reference may be required.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MSLTPrac graduates will have advanced knowledge and comprehension of SLTPrac theory, applications and practice, They will be able to diagnose communication problems, apply clinical theory to practice and interact with other health professionals in a variety of settings.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5119"},"OO0503":{"i":"OO0503","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor of Medicine and Bachelor of Surgery degree of a university in New Zealand, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this degree programme will be prepared for professional behaviours and activities consistent with working at a consultant level in an aeromedical retrieval and transport setting, by inculcating a range of competencies, knowledge and attitudes that only arise from specialist practice.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0503"},"OO0538":{"i":"OO0538","entryRequirements":"NZ registered nurse with current practising certificate; minimum of 3 years practice within the past 5 years; and PGDipHealSc  with B grade average.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this degree programme will have advanced knowledge and mastery of sophisticated theoretical subject matter, the ability to undertake autonomous scholarship, and the ability to independently undertake research and translate the findings into practice. The programme will enable registered nurses to enter the health professional scope of NP registration under the HPCAA 2003.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0538"},"OO0421":{"i":"OO0421","entryRequirements":"A Degree or appropriate alternative qualification","strategicPurposeStatement":"This certificate is designed to develop the relevant skills for family planning trainees, midwives, general practitioners.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0421"},"OO0243":{"i":"OO0243","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Dental Surgery","strategicPurposeStatement":"This diploma provides study, practical training and an introduction to research in designated areas of community dentistry. Recipients can proceed to further postgraduate study.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0243"},"MY0243":{"i":"MY0243","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelor's degree and professional experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Holders will have advanced knowledge and skills in the purpose, practice and philosophy in the field of rehabilitation.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0243"},"OO0466":{"i":"OO0466","entryRequirements":"Postgraduate Diploma in Dietetics or equivalent qualification, plus professional registration in Dietetics.","strategicPurposeStatement":"This degree provides in-depth study in an area of Dietetics. It provides advanced knowledge in the field and the ability to study independently.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0466"},"AK1025":{"i":"AK1025","entryRequirements":"Bachelor's degree or equivalent, plus evidence of current professional practice.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PA pathway of study for professionals that is applied and practice oriented, focusing on psychological and societal responses to emergencies within communities.  International trends are also explored.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1025"},"HB3963":{"i":"HB3963","strategicPurposeStatement":"To enable health professionals to develop skills of research, critical analysis, constructive synthesis and advanced practice","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Certificate in Health Science will  \n\r\nhave developed their knowledge and skills of critical analysis,  \n\r\nconstructive synthesis and their application to high quality  \n\r\napproaches to health care delivery.","educationPathway":"Pending successful completion of the required academic entry  \n\r\nrequirements, graduates of the Postgraduate Certificate in Health  \n\r\nScience may progress to the Postgraduate Diploma in Health Science, or  \n\r\nMaster of Health Science. Registered Nurse graduates may progress to  \n\r\nthe Master of Nursing.","developedBy":"Eastern Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=HB3963"},"OO0196":{"i":"OO0196","entryRequirements":"Postgraduate diploma in General Practice and registration as a medical practitioner; 2 years experience in General Practice or  training in General Practice","strategicPurposeStatement":"This degree is for general practitioners seeking postgraduate study. It involves in-depth study and supervised research. It provides advanced knowledge in the field and the ability to study independently and carry out original research.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0196"},"AK3825":{"i":"AK3825","entryRequirements":"A Master of Psychotherapy or equivalent, plus registration.","strategicPurposeStatement":"This programme has been designed to meet and balance various needs and requirements. In particular it will provide the knowledge required for work with infants, children, adolescent families and whanau in various contexts in Aotearoa New Zealand and which, therefore, acknowledges Te Tiriti o Waitangi as a basis for partnership with tangata whenua. It will also develop the student's ability to work professionally in a way that meets national and international standards for child and adolescent psychotherapy.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK3825"},"AU5521":{"i":"AU5521","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Pharmacy or an equivalent pharmacy qualification and registration as a pharmacist in New Zealand or in the country of domicile.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Pharmacists who complete the PGDipClinPharm will have greater experience in the preparation and implementation of pharmaceutical care and medicines management plans for a wide range of therapeutic areas, and for patients with more complex clinical needs. They will have a degree of specialisation to facilitate the progress to advanced clinical roles.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5521"},"MY0223":{"i":"MY0223","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Veterinary Science degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will demonstrate advanced knowledge and skills in areas of Veterinary Science. They will be able to critically evaluate information and communicate effectively, and be prepared for further study or employment. They will have good quantitative skills, be able to solve a range of both theoretical and practical problems, have acquired the ability to work independently and with groups, and where relevant to the discipline analyse data appropriately.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0223"},"VI001K":{"i":"VI001K","entryRequirements":"A bachelors degree with honours or a postgraduate diploma (or equivalent) in a health-related discipline. Candidates in nursing or midwifery must hold the relevant professional registration.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will show evidence of advanced knowledge in their specialist field of professional health practice. They will be able to critically evaluate the literature; research, analyse and argue from evidence; and show mastery of theoretical concepts relevant to their discipline. They will demonstrate the capacity for independent thinking through the design and conduct of a piece of supervised research, and be ready to apply these skills to new situations in existing or new roles in the health sector. Some graduates may be able to continue to further study at doctoral level.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI001K"},"CN0947":{"i":"CN0947","entryRequirements":"An approved Bachelor's degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this programme will be able to demonstrate advanced knowledge and skills, developed through theoretical courses, scholarly inquiry, evidence-based research and clinical practice to work autonomously and independently in collaborative allied health teams. The study and clinical practice hours may contri","graduateProfile":"A range of assessments will be used including written assignments, quizzes, presentations, reflections, practical assignments, group work and viva.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0947"},"OO0413":{"i":"OO0413","entryRequirements":"Appropriate degree in Medicine and registration for Medical Practice","strategicPurposeStatement":"This postgraduate diploma is an internationally recognised qualification in ophthalmic basic sciences.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0413"},"AU5552":{"i":"AU5552","entryRequirements":"In order to be admitted to this programme a student needs to have completed the requirements for a Bachelors degree","strategicPurposeStatement":"To enable health professionals to achieve mastery of health leadership and management principles.","graduateProfile":"Not applicable","educationPathway":"Not applicable","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5552"},"MY0358":{"i":"MY0358","entryRequirements":"Bachelors degree with a grade average of B- in the highest level papers.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates from the Massey University Master of Sport Management degree programme will: * Have further developed their in-depth knowledge and skills in sport management, either through professional experience or professional educational programmes in areas related to sport management. * Have developed an understanding about the structure and essence of sport throughout New Zealand. * Have gained practical work experience in the sport industry in New Zealand. * Have gained exposure to sport industry professionals through in-class guest lectures, field trips, internships, and researching for assignments. * Have developed an international perspective on sport management. * Be able to work independently and in teams and to interact effectively with colleagues, clients and other professionals in the field. * Be practised in clearly and concisely communicating the findings of an investigation in oral and written form. *Have completed and presented a report on professional practice experience. A graduate of the Master of Sport Management with a class of Honours will be able to proceed to research master degrees, for research training, and thence to doctoral study.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0358"},"OO0041":{"i":"OO0041","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Medicine and Bachelor of Surgery degrees plus appropriate experience","strategicPurposeStatement":"This diploma involves community aspects of child health, and the development of clinical knowledge and skills concerning paediatrics and child health appropriate for a general practitioner with a special interest in children.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0041"},"OO0436":{"i":"OO0436","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Medicine and Bachelor of Surgery obtained in New Zealand, or equivalent. Applicants will be selected on the basis of their ability and experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Holders of this diploma will have undertaken adequate scientific training and acquired sufficient skills to work safely as the medical adviser to a range of industries.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0436"},"CN0524":{"i":"CN0524","entryRequirements":"An approved Bachelor's degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be prepared with the public health knowledge and skills to work in a multi-cultural society, applying a critical understanding of their responsibilities to Te Tiriti. They will have applied public health knowledge to analyse data and critically assess evidence-based interventions to improve population health outcomes.","graduateProfile":"A range of assessments will be used including written assignments, presentations, reflections, practical assignments, and group work.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0524"},"AU5739":{"i":"AU5739","entryRequirements":"Completed the requirements for a Bachelors Honours degree, Masters degree or postgraduate diploma in a relevant subject with a minimum GPA, or completed the requirements for a Bachelor of Medicine and Bachelor of Surgery, and have the research experience, ability, and disciplinary training to undertake doctoral level research.","strategicPurposeStatement":"DHSc graduates will be provided with advanced academic preparation for service leadership and academic roles. They will enhance their skills to lead health service delivery to meet diverse health needs of the population prioritising Maori and Pacific within an inter-disciplinary context across acute and primary / community care settings. They will demonstrate an advanced, flexible and analytical approach to generate, critique and utilise knowledge, and contribute to the evidence base of health care practice and delivery through world leading and innovative research.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5739"},"AK3930":{"i":"AK3930","strategicPurposeStatement":"MDRMD graduates will have an advanced understanding of the psychological behaviours and societal factors in the causation of and response to emergencies.  A progression of study aligned to the CDEM Act 2002 to educate professionals in the psychological behaviours and societal factors in the causation of and response to emergencies","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK3930"},"OO0223":{"i":"OO0223","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Pharmacy degree or Bachelor of Pharmacy with Honours or acceptable experience/qualifications plus registration as a Pharmacist","strategicPurposeStatement":"This diploma provides study, practical training and an introduction to research in designated areas of clinical pharmacy. Recipients can proceed to further postgraduate study.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0223"},"AK3485":{"i":"AK3485","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelor's degree completed to a merit standard.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MHSc graduates will have advanced knowledge and understanding in their chosen health profession to help improve the efficiency, effectiveness and quality of the health care profession and better meet consumer needs. They will be critical and reflective, with strong applied research capability. They will have demonstrated the ability to engage in a sustained period of research, and may progress to further study at doctoral level.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK3485"},"OO0487":{"i":"OO0487","entryRequirements":"A Postgraduate Diploma in Clinical Pharmacy or equivalent qualification; current registration as a pharmacist in New Zealand; an appropriate position involving patient care; access to a designated medical prescriber.","strategicPurposeStatement":"This certificate programme provides registered pharmacists with the knowledge and skills needed to register as pharmacist prescribers with the Pharmacy Council of New Zealand. Holders of the certificate will be able to demonstrate comprehensive pharmacotherapeutic knowledge of medicines within their proposed area(s) of prescribing practice; access and evaluate relevant clinical information concerning individual patients in order to prescribe safely and effectively; demonstrate skills in patient assessment, diagnosis and clinical decision-making to facilitate good prescribing decisions; and demonstrate competence in prescribing practice under supervision.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0487"},"OO0443":{"i":"OO0443","entryRequirements":"A relevant Bachelor's degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be technicians with advanced training in cardiology or sleep medicine. They will be reflective practitioners who can evaluate, judge and adapt to the changes and challenges presented by clinical practice.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0443"},"OO0036":{"i":"OO0036","entryRequirements":"Completion of 3rd or 5th year of Bachelor of Medicine and Bachelor of Surgery degrees.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Bachelor of Medical Science with Honours (BMedSc(Hons)) degree is available for medical students who may apply to take this research degree after satisfactorily completing three or more years of the medical degree (MB ChB). Most students elect to take the BMedSc(Hons) year after the third year of the medical degree but a few do so after the fifth year, prior to the trainee intern year.This in-depth study stands graduates in good stead for a future career involving research or academic medicine.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0036"},"OT4864":{"i":"OT4864","entryRequirements":"Selection will be made on the basis of the following criteria: \n\r\nregistered midwife, and \n\r\nBachelor's degree or equivalent, or \n\r\nPostgraduate Certificate in Midwifery Practice or equivalent. \n\n\n\r\nAdmission Procedure\n\r\nApplicants will make an application using the Otago Polytechnic online application process.  Those seeking admission via a portfolio application will need to provide their CV and portfolio with the application form. \n\n\n\r\nThe Postgraduate Programme Leader or Head of School will assess the portfolio against the portfolio criteria of the courses or programmes for which the ākonga has applied. Assessment of some aspects of portfolio applications may be through interview.\n\n\n\r\nAll documents in support of an application for recognition of prior learning cross credit or portfolio must be verified by a JP or an institutional e-Qual verification service.\n\n\n\r\nInternational student language requirements\n\n\n\r\nThe same entry criteria apply to international ākonga.  New Zealand registered kahu pōkai | midwives for whom English is a second language are admitted using the Midwifery Council of New Zealand requirements i.e. to have an IELTS score of 7.0 or Occupational English Test (OET) minimum pass mark of A or B in each section. International midwifery ākonga who are not registered in New Zealand will require an IELTS score of 7.5, with no less than 7.0 in any band, or an OET score of A or B in each section","strategicPurposeStatement":"To produce graduates who can extend and deepen their knowledge of the theories and procedures used in the midwifery practice environment, in a wider and more encompassing scope than in the postgraduate certificate. This includes an enhanced understanding of the roles of those with whom they work. Graduates will have completed a further four practice courses or, theory and research methods courses to prepare them for masters study","graduateProfile":"On completion of the Postgraduate Diploma in Midwifery ākonga will be able to:  \n\r\n1) Apply enhanced knowledge and understanding on which to: \n\r\n* assess and manage clinical situations, \n\r\n* develop creative and innovative approaches to midwifery practice, and \n\r\n* manage change and uncertainty in midwifery and perinatal care. \n\r\n2) Apply advanced skills of critique and analysis enabling: \n\r\n* effective problem solving, \n\r\n* development of evidence-based practice guidelines, \n\r\n* safe and effective care which improves outcomes for women/people and their pēpi/babies, \n\r\n* critique of major theoretical positions pertaining to midwifery and perinatal care, and \n\r\n* an appreciation of the impact of broad health policy on midwifery and perinatal care. \n\r\n3) Apply advanced communication skills and the ability to work in partnership with women/people/whānau. \n\r\n4) Use critical reflection and self-knowledge as tools for continuing critique and enhancement of own clinical practice. \n\r\n5) Apply personal insight and independent thinking to professional and personal development. \n\r\n6) Apply knowledge and skill to: \n\r\n* guide and support midwifery colleagues,  \n\r\n* participate actively in the midwifery profession, \n\r\n* maintain a midwifery focus within a collaborative and interdisciplinary context, and \n\r\n* identify clinical or professional issues requiring investigation and research.","educationPathway":"The programme provides a pathway into master's studies in midwifery.","developedBy":"Otago Polytechnic","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OT4864"},"AU5558":{"i":"AU5558","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor of Nursing, or equivalent, with a minimum GPA, registration as a nurse in New Zealand, at least two years' post-registration clinical practice experience; or overseas registration and two years' post-registration clinical practice experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have developed a set of knowledge and skills in clinical inquiry, critical appraisal and scholarship and the ability to introduce change to effect positive outcomes for patient groups/populations. Enabling them to undertake innovative, specialist roles in clinical practice such as designated prescriber, and provide leadership to other nurses and the health care team.","graduateProfile":"NA","educationPathway":"NA","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5558"},"CN0218":{"i":"CN0218","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be eligible to register as Psychologists under the general scope of the New Zealand Psychologists Board","graduateProfile":"A range of assessments will be used including a final oral exam, coursework submitted throughout programme, field supervisor reports and reflective journals.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0218"},"OO0048":{"i":"OO0048","entryRequirements":"A medical qualification plus medical experience","strategicPurposeStatement":"This diploma offers occupational health training to registered medical practitioners.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0048"},"MY0417":{"i":"MY0417","entryRequirements":"Bachelor's degree in Veterinary Science or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MVS graduates will have knowledge at a high level in a veterinary science discipline. They will be able to create new knowledge, critically evaluate information and communicate effectively, and be prepared for doctoral study or employment. They will have good quantitative skills, be able to solve a range of both theoretical and practical problems, have acquired the ability to work independently and with groups and, where relevant to the discipline, be able to design experiments and analyse data appropriately.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0417"},"AK3840":{"i":"AK3840","strategicPurposeStatement":"MPhyPrac graduates will be eligible to apply for registration with the New Zealand Physiotherapy Board. They will be academically, technically, and clinically competent. They will be able to adapt to new challenges and contribute to the profession of physiotherapy as consumers and creators of high-quality research. They will be critical and reflective practitioners able to pursue further postgraduate study","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK3840"},"WK2484":{"i":"WK2484","entryRequirements":"Applicants are required to have gained an undergraduate degree in Sport and Exercise Science conferred by a New Zealand tertiary education institution, or a qualification, industry experience and / or informal transfer of credit approved as equivalent by the Sport Science Postgraduate Programme Committee.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have postgraduate knowledge and skills including critical analysis and reflection to enhance career prospects and opportunities in sport, health, fitness & recreation industries.","developedBy":"Waikato Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Quality Assurance Division, NZQA","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WK2484"},"OO0423":{"i":"OO0423","entryRequirements":"A postgraduate Diploma in Ophthalmic Basic Sciences and a medical degree","strategicPurposeStatement":"This degree provides advance training in Ophthlamic research.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0423"},"CN0928":{"i":"CN0928","entryRequirements":"Bachelor's degree with Honours or Master's degree plus a minimum of five years' experience in a relevant professional practice role.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the Doctor of Health Sciences will effectively generate and utilise health data and research to inform, develop and potentially change professional practice and health systems to improve the outcomes and experiences of health consumers, whanau and communities. They will demonstrate critical application of bicultural competence in the process of research development and design.    \n\n\n\r\nThey will provide leadership to the health workforce and their professional communities in generating and applying research that extends the boundaries of knowledge, informs health policy and system transformation, and promotes strategies to reduce inequities in health outcomes.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0928"},"OO0222":{"i":"OO0222","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Pharmacy degree or Bachelor of Pharmacy with Honours or acceptable experience/qualifications","strategicPurposeStatement":"This diploma provides study, practical training and an introduction to research in designated areas of pharmacy. Recipients can proceed to further postgraduate study.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0222"},"AU5038":{"i":"AU5038","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor of Nursing, Bachelor of Nursing (Honours) or Postgraduate Diploma in Health Sciences, with a minimum GPA, or its equivalent, and registration as a nurse in New Zealand.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MNurs graduates will be prepared as advanced practitioners able to work in a range of health settings with different client populations.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5038"},"AU5164":{"i":"AU5164","entryRequirements":"Bachelor's degree or overseas equivalent, or a professional qualification with two years relevant work experience in a health related discipline, and currently engaged in clinical teaching or curriculum development.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGDipClinEd graduates will understand the principles of adult learning within the healthcare context. They will be skilled at curriculum planning, evaluation and assessment and will demonstrate their position as leaders and innovators in health professionals education.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5164"},"OO0475":{"i":"OO0475","entryRequirements":"The degrees of Bachelor of Medicine and Bachelor of Surgery from a university in New Zealand (or an approved equivalent medical qualification), and previous relevant training and experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Postgraduate Diploma in Surgical Anatomy (PGDipSurgAnat) graduates will be medical professionals with a sound working knowledge of topographical anatomy appropriate to safe and competent surgical/interventional practice. They will be able to critically assimilate and apply anatomical information to practical diagnostic and therapeutic procedures, and have the skills to communicate anatomical concepts clearly and concisely to a variety of audiences.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0475"},"HB3849":{"i":"HB3849","entryRequirements":"15.2 Admission Requirements 15.2.1 Entry to the Postgraduate Certificate/Diploma of Health Science programme may be limited by the number of places available; places may be apportioned between different categories of eligibility and modes of study. Applicants who meet the entry requirements may be accepted onto the Programmes until maximum class sizes are reached. 15.2.2 The academic entry requirement for the Certificate/Diploma of Health Science is one of the following: * an NZQF-listed undergraduate degree (or equivalent) in a health-related field with a minimum of the equivalent to a B average as per the EIT-specified 11-point achievement-based grading system; or * a degree or equivalent professional qualification in a different field if the applicant can supply evidence of work experience at degree level or above within a health related field, subject to an interview and/or the submission of a portfolio of evidence to establish the status and relevance of the applicant's prior learning and experience; or * at the Dean's discretion, where an applicant's situation is compelling but not covered by the requirements listed above. 15.2.3 Additional entry requirements for the specified nursing practice endorsements are as follows: * Registered Nurse * Current annual practising certificate from the Nursing Council of New Zealand 15.2.4 Applicants from countries in which English is not the primary spoken language must demonstrate an acceptable level of English language fluency prior to acceptance in the programme. Ways in which English language fluency may be demonstrated include (i) completion of a programme of study in which English was the language of instruction (conditions apply*), and (ii) approved scores on IELTS tests, namely an Academic score of 6.5 with no band lower than 6 (or accepted international equivalents). *See NZQA English language entry requirements for international students at \nhere\n 15.2.5 An international student must be in possession of an appropriate visa for the duration of the Programme.","strategicPurposeStatement":"To enable health professions to develop skills of research, critical analysis, constructive synthesis and advanced practise in their discipline.","graduateProfile":"Completion of the programme contributes towards graduates' ability to: - articulate the scope of their practice and its advancement; - apply a broad body of advanced knowledge, scholarship, and skills within their scopes of professional practice; - critically evaluate their own practice and that of others; - lead collaborative expert practice across settings within an interdisciplinary team; - act as a consultant, leader, role model, mentor, and teacher in complex situations and across disciplines; - influence and contribute to the development of health and socio-economic policies at a local and national level; and - research, critically analyse, and implement findings in practice, advancing knowledge and understanding.","educationPathway":"Masters' programmes","developedBy":"Eastern Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=HB3849"},"OT4865":{"i":"OT4865","entryRequirements":"Selection will be made on the basis of the following criteria:\n\r\n*\tregistered midwife, and\n\r\n*\tPostgraduate Diploma in Midwifery with B grade average, or equivalent.\n\n\n\r\nMaster of Midwifery (by portfolio, 180 credits)\n\r\nConsideration for direct entry into the 180 credit thesis pathway will require presentation of a portfolio which demonstrates academic and personal skills appropriate for enrolment in a 180 credit Master's programme.\n\n\n\r\nThese may include:\n\r\n*\tEligibility for cross crediting of postgraduate level courses completed elsewhere\n\r\n*\tPortfolio of publications \n\r\n*\tCompletion of 60 credits of postgraduate study or its equivalent\n\r\n*\tPresentation of a comprehensive and well-structured research proposal\n\r\n*\tCompleted research projects or ongoing involvement in collaborative research projects which demonstrate understanding and facility with research processes\n\r\n*\tMidwifery experience which could include an extensive practice history including project work undertaken during self, or institutional employment.\n\n\n\r\nAdmission Procedure\n\r\nApplicants will make an application using the Otago Polytechnic online application process.  Those seeking admission via a portfolio application will need to provide their CV and portfolio with the application form. \n\n\n\r\nThe Postgraduate Programme Leader or Head of School will assess the portfolio against the portfolio criteria of the courses or programmes for which the ākonga has applied. Assessment of some aspects of portfolio applications may be through interview.\n\n\n\r\nAll documents in support of an application for recognition of prior learning cross credit or portfolio must be verified by a JP or an institutional e-Qual verification service.\n\n\n\r\nInternational student language requirements\n\r\nThe same entry criteria apply to international ākonga.  New Zealand registered kahu pōkai | midwives for whom English is a second language are admitted using the Midwifery Council of New Zealand requirements i.e. to have an IELTS score of 7.0 or Occupational English Test (OET) minimum pass mark of A or B in each section. International midwifery ākonga who are not registered in New Zealand will require an IELTS score of 7.5, with no less than 7.0 in any band, or an OET score of A or B in each section.","strategicPurposeStatement":"To produce graduates who will demonstrate mastery of theoretical and sophisticated subject matter through a body of scholarly applied work in the form of a thesis or other negotiated research output, which will form the basis of scholarly journal articles and national and international conference presentations. The work will respond to societal needs, address practice from multiple perspectives positioned within a wider framework of academic and applied research. This qualification prepares learners for doctoral level study.","graduateProfile":"On completion of the Master of Midwifery akonga will be able to apply: \n\r\n1) Advanced knowledge and understanding of the theoretical and practice issues in midwifery on which to \n\r\n* assess and manage clinical situations,  \n\r\n* develop creative and innovative approaches to midwifery practice, and \n\r\n* manage change and uncertainty in midwifery. \n\n\n\n\n\r\n2) Develop midwifery knowledge and practice through research and scholarly inquiry. \n\n\n\r\n3) Apply the skills of critique and analysis enabling \n\r\n* effective problem solving, \n\r\n* development of evidence-based practice guidelines, \n\r\n* safe and effective care which improves outcomes for women/people and their pēpi/babies, \n\r\n* critique of major theoretical positions pertaining to midwifery, and \n\r\n* an appreciation of the impact of broad health policy and directions on midwifery and perinatal care. \n\n\n\r\n4) Complete (to internationally recognised standards) a piece of original research or scholarship, which includes higher order skills in analysis and critical evaluation. \n\n\n\r\n5) Apply advanced communication skills and the ability to work in partnership with women/people/whānau. \n\n\n\r\n6) Use critical reflection and self-knowledge as tools for continuing critique and enhancement of own clinical practice. \n\n\n\r\n7) Model, professional and personal development. \n\n\n\r\n8) Apply knowledge and skill to: \n\r\n* provide guidance and support for midwifery colleagues, \n\r\n* take a leadership role in the midwifery profession, \n\r\n* develop professional networks both at local, national and international levels, \n\r\n* act as a change agent in the provision of midwifery services including involvement in the development of health policy, \n\r\n* maintain a midwifery focus within a collaborative and interdisciplinary context, and \n\r\n* identify clinical or professional issues requiring investigation and research.","educationPathway":"Graduates of this programme may be able to pathway into doctoral studies.","developedBy":"Otago Polytechnic","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OT4865"},"OT4807":{"i":"OT4807","entryRequirements":"Applicants for the Masters of Occupational Therapy commencing at level 9 can enter by any of the following pathways:\n\r\nBachelor of Occupational Therapy (- Honours) or equivalent: \n\r\nApplicants must have: \n\r\n- Completed a discrete 120 credit Honours following a Bachelor of Occupational Therapy, OR a four-year Honours degree in occupational therapy or equivalent, in which they have individually completed a small-scale research project and undertaken a research course (normally 50% of their final year of study) \n\r\n- Achieved a First Class Hons or Second Class Hons, First Division (2:1) or equivalent.\n\r\nPostgraduate Certificate in Occupational Therapy Practice or Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Practice in Health and Wellbeing (Specialty) or The Postgraduate Diploma in Occupational Therapy Practice \n\r\n- Must have a minimum of a B grade average over 60 credits at Level 8\n\n\n\r\nWhen entering at Level 8 ākonga can select the appropriate pathway listed below and provide the relevant evidence: \n\r\nPathway One - Research thesis -- They will have: \n\r\n- Successfully completed 60 credits at level 8 of relevant study \n\r\n- B grade average across the 60 credits \n\r\n- Successfully completed MO435001 Research for Practice or equivalent 30 credit course \n\n\n\r\nPathway Two - Research Dissertation - They will have \n\r\n- Successfully completed 90 credits at level 8 of relevant study \n\r\n- B grade average across their best 60 credits \n\r\n- Successfully completed MO435001 Research for Practice or equivalent 30 credit course \n\n\n\r\nPathway Three - Research Project They will have:\n\r\n - Successfully completed 120 credits at level 8 of relevant study \n\r\n- B grade average across their best 60 credits \n\r\n- Successfully completed MO435001 Research for Practice or equivalent 30 credit course.\n\n\n\r\nAdditionally, a candidate's prior qualification should have been completed no more than five years prior, the programme leader will assess the qualification to make the final determination.\n\r\nInternational applicants for whom English is a second language are required to have an IELTS overall band score (Academic) of 6.5 with a minimum score of 6.5 in each band. These IELTS scores align with what is required to apply for registration as an occupational therapist in Aotearoa New Zealand. \n\n\n\r\nApplicants who do not meet all of the requirements for entry into the programme can make an application to the Head of School, who will consider the application on a case-by-case basis. Entry to the programme will be at the Head of School's discretion.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The aim of the Master of Occupational Therapy is to produce graduates that demonstrate expert knowledge and leadership in an area of practice. Graduates will have conducted independent research in a chosen area to advance professional theory and practice. They will have demonstrable research and analytical skills which can be used to advance evidence-informed practice in practice or academic roles. Graduates will be equipped to apply their advanced knowledge to influence policy, conduct further research or pursue further academic study in Aotearoa New Zealand's bicultural context.","graduateProfile":"By the end of this programme, graduates will be able to: \n\r\n- Critically evaluate relevant literature and research, applying advanced contemporary knowledge to improve their own and others' occupational therapy interventions being offered in Aotearoa New Zealand's bicultural context \n\r\n- Conduct research, analyse findings, and disseminate findings within occupational therapy and academic communities. \n\r\n- Advocate for and conduct ongoing research for the advancement of knowledge in specialist fields of occupational therapy.","educationPathway":"Most students undertaking postgraduate studies within the School of Occupational Therapy are already employed, a small number are using postgraduate study to update their knowledge and skills to enable them to return to, or gain entry into the workforce.   \n\r\nCompletion of a qualification can provide graduates with:   \n\r\n* evidence to support advancement within their chosen career pathway   \n\r\n* the knowledge and skills to  seek employment in a specialty area of practice, or to advance into leadership positions  \n\r\n* the skills to seek employment in  an educational institution or seek a position that involves research   \n\r\n* the knowledge, skills and confidence  to work in non-traditional or emergent areas of practice.","developedBy":"Otago Polytechnic","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OT4807"},"OO0406":{"i":"OO0406","entryRequirements":"Degree or appropriate alternative qualification","strategicPurposeStatement":"This postgraduate certificate provides a formal nationally recognised qualification for health professionals who practise in the field of Travel and Migrant Medicine.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0406"},"VI00Y1":{"i":"VI00Y1","entryRequirements":"A bachelors degree in a health-related discipline, registration as a health professional, and work experience in health care.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have an advanced understanding of health care systems and will use their skills to improve health care outcomes in their chosen health specialty. They will be able to advance their career in their health field. Graduates can progress to further study in the Postgraduate Diploma in Health Care and then to the Master of Health Care.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00Y1"},"MY0241":{"i":"MY0241","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelor's degree and professional experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Holders will have developed knowledge and skills in the theory and practice of cognitive behaviour therapy.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0241"},"MY0416":{"i":"MY0416","entryRequirements":"Bachelor's degree in Veterinary Science or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MVSc graduates will have knowledge at a higher level than a BVSc graduate in a veterinary science discipline. They will be able to create new knowledge, critically evaluate information and communicate effectively, and be prepared for doctoral study or employment. They will have good quantitative skills, be able to solve a range of both theoretical and practical problems, have acquired the ability to work independently and with groups and, where relevant to the discipline, be able to design experiments and analyse data appropriately.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0416"},"VI005R":{"i":"VI005R","entryRequirements":"Direct entry to the Master of Physical Activity and Hauora requires a bachelor's degree in a relevant discipline, (for example: Health, Sport Science, Exercise Physiology or Physical Education) with an average grade of B. These requirements can be waived by the Associate Dean (students) for a candidate who has had extensive practical, professional or cultural experience of an appropriate level.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the Master of Physical Activity and Hauora will have advanced skills to lead change amongst health promotion colleagues and communities. They will be critical thinkers that bring innovation and social justice to policy and community development. Graduates will have advanced skills in applying evidence-based practice and matauranga Maori as well as evaluating, explaining, and improving health promotion knowledge in the physical activity sector of Aotearoa New Zealand and internationally.","graduateProfile":"Assessment will be through a variety of items of written, creative, and oral work including annotated bibliographies and literature reviews, creative and cultural works, expositions of practice issues, research and evaluation proposals, essays, case studies, action learning plans, and project and other reflective reports. Students will also be assessed on their skills in completing and reporting on their own research / evaluation project. In addition, students' in-class presentations, and participation in online discussions and tutorials will contribute to assessment in some courses.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI005R"},"HB3911":{"i":"HB3911","entryRequirements":"The academic entry requirement for the MN is one of the following: * completion of the HB3963 Postgraduate Diploma in Health Science (Registered Nurse Prescribing endorsement) with a B average or higher; or * a postgraduate nursing qualification deemed equivalent to the HB3963 Postgraduate Diploma in Health Science (Registered Nurse Prescribing endorsement) with a B average or higher; or * at the Dean's discretion, where an applicant's situation is compelling but not covered by the requirements listed above. Normally, enrolment into the MN programme will be through the HB3963 Postgraduate Diploma in Health Science (Registered Nurse Prescribing endorsement). A minimum B average is required for confirmation of enrolment into the MN. Additional entry requirements for the MN are specified as follows by the NCNZ: * The applicant must be an RN with a current New Zealand practising certificate and be in good standing with the Council. * The applicant must have completed a minimum of three years' equivalent full-time relevant practice within the last five years (with at least one of the three years in full-time practice in New Zealand) in the intended area of practice as an NP. Applicants from countries in which English is not the primary spoken language must demonstrate an acceptable level of English language fluency prior to acceptance in the programme. Ways in which English language fluency may be demonstrated include (i) completion of a programme of study in which English was the language of instruction (conditions apply ), and (ii) approved scores on IELTS tests, namely an Academic score of 7 for reading, listening and speaking and a minimum score of 6.5 for writing (or accepted international equivalents e.g. OET a minimum score of 350 for reading, listening and speaking and minimum score of 300 for writing).","strategicPurposeStatement":"To enable students to develop advanced knowledge & skills in health science related to their individual disciplines & scope of practice through intensive academic study, including advanced independent work, advanced practice, and research.","graduateProfile":"EIT's Master of Nursing programme will enhance your nursing knowledge, skills in critical analysis, constructive synthesis, along with advanced practice and research within your specialty area, particularly in preparation for advanced practice roles.*  \n\n\n\r\n*EIT's Master of Nursing qualification has been approved by the Nursing Council of New Zealand as a \"masters with a clinical focus, including the content for preparation for nurse prescribing\" - for graduates to become nurse practitioners.","educationPathway":"Further studies in related fields","developedBy":"Eastern Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=HB3911"},"OO0238":{"i":"OO0238","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor of Physiotherapy degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"This diploma programme involves advanced study, practical training and an introduction to research in designated areas of physiotherapy. Recipients of the diploma can proceed to further postgraduate study.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0238"},"OO0544":{"i":"OO0544","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree in Information Science, Computer Science, Health Sciences, or an acceptable equivalent qualification.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will understand how to critically evaluate and communicate the principles of Digital Health demonstrating enhanced theoretical and technical knowledge of the specialty.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0544"},"OO0444":{"i":"OO0444","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor's degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be rehabilitation professionals equipped with a sound understanding of the priniciples and theories underpinning rehabiliation practice. They will be able to integrate current theory and research into their practice along with an understanding of the ethics involved with working in a professional practice environment. Completion of this certificate also provides an entry point to postgraduate education for health professionals and others working in the field of rehabilitation.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0444"},"OO0408":{"i":"OO0408","entryRequirements":"A medical degree or equivalent, registration for medical practice, and two years of approved experience in general practice.","strategicPurposeStatement":"This postgraduate certificate provides a formal nationally recognised qualification for medical practitioners who staff rural hospitals.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0408"},"MY0340":{"i":"MY0340","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelor's degree and at least 2 years' practice as a registered nurse within 5 years of application.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have knowledge and skills for advanced nursing practice within a particular scope of practice, acquired through theoretical papers, clinical practice and scholarly enquiry.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0340"},"WI1013":{"i":"WI1013","entryRequirements":"Bachelors degree in a relevant subject with at least a B grade average across the 300 level papers or equivalent, by selection process to ensure admission criteria is met by the University, and for registration to the Midwifery Council of New Zealand, and be registered with one of the professions regulated under the Health Practitioners Competence Assurance Act 2003.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the Master of Clinical Practice (Midwifery) will be eligible to apply for registration as a midwife in Aotearoa New Zealand upon successful completion of the National Midwifery Examination. They will be qualified to work in all new graduate midwifery settings. Graduates will be well prepared for further postgraduate studies in midwifery and other related areas.","graduateProfile":"Examination or internal assessment","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI1013"},"MY0339":{"i":"MY0339","entryRequirements":"Admission to the Degree of Master of Clinical Practice (Nursing) requires that the candidate will: \n\n\n\r\n(a) meet the University admission requirements as specified; \n\n\n\r\n(b) have been awarded or qualified for a Bachelor's degree or an equivalent qualification with a grade average of at least a B over the highest two levels of courses; \n\n\n\r\n(c) meet Health Clearance and Police Vetting requirements as specified by the Academic Board or their delegate; \n\n\n\r\n(d) meet the requirements for registration as a nurse in New Zealand as set down by the Nursing Council of New Zealand in terms of good character and fitness to be a nurse; \n\n\n\r\n(e) have achieved an IELTS of 7 with no band less than 7 within the preceding three months, if English is not the applicant's first language and the language of instruction in previous schooling is not English; and \n\n\n\r\n(f) be selected into the programme on the basis of a selection process which includes a written application, and may include an interview and practical exercises as determined by the Academic Board or their delegate.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Master of Clinical Practice (Nursing), graduates will: \n\r\nPersonal capabilities \n\r\n1.    Be innovative and implement new ways of working. \n\r\n2.    Be a reflective, proactive, self-directed, lifelong learner. \n\r\n - Discipline-specific competencies \n\r\n1.    Demonstrate professional responsibility; management of nursing care; and skilful interpersonal relationships with people and whanau in an interprofessional context. \n\r\n2.    Demonstrate professional competence based on evidence-based practice. \n\r\n3.    Apply skills of direction and delegation in determining the appropriate level of care required.  \n\r\n4.    Apply ethical analysis and clinical reasoning to assessment, intervention and evaluation of nursing care. \n\r\n - Professional attributes \n\r\n1.    Demonstrate leadership in collaboration across the health care sector. \n\r\n2.    Demonstrate interpersonal skills by connecting, enabling, and engaging with health consumers and their whanau to support their health and wellbeing.  \n\r\n3.    Apply critical reflective analysis to their own and others' professional practice. \n\r\n4.    Contribute in a scholarly way to the personal and professional nature of nursing. \n\r\n - Ethical and social attributes \n\r\n1.    Demonstrate critical understanding of the relevance of the Treaty of Waitangi and incorporate its principles in the Nursing practice. \n\r\n2.    Respect diverse cultural values and beliefs, promoting an equitable health care system and advocating for health consumers and their whanau when concerns arise. \n\r\n3.    Integrate the legal and ethical codes of practice into their Nursing role. \n\r\n4.    Synthesise evidence and knowledge to promote planetary health and sustainable development for all.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0339"},"VI00X5":{"i":"VI00X5","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree and New Zealand Registered Nurse status.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be leaders in their clinical environments and will have advanced clinical and research skills. They will be prepared to improve health outcomes through their knowledge and critique of current practice issues, advanced clinical reasoning and understanding of the application of research to practice. The Master of Nursing Science may lead to a PhD. Employment opportunities include Clinical Nurse Specialist, academic, research or management roles, and for some graduates advancement to Nurse Practitioner status.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00X5"},"AK3733":{"i":"AK3733","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree and three years' professional experience, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MHPrac graduates will be health professionals in clinical practice who have developed advanced practice to ensure current and appropriate specialist health services are provided to clients.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK3733"},"MY1014":{"i":"MY1014","entryRequirements":"Appropriate degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will participate and collaborate with colleagues in health and health care education, promotion and practice. They will apply knowledge of health science in its broadest perspective and at a specialty level. They will value and uphold diverse approaches to health and health care, and be able to contribute to public debate on health related issues.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY1014"},"AU0436":{"i":"AU0436","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Medicine and Bachelor of Surgery, and Postgraduate Diploma in Medical Science or Bachelor of Human Biology (Honours), and current registration with NZ Medical Council","strategicPurposeStatement":"MMedSc graduates will have advanced knowledge, skills and research capabilities to enable them to demonstrate critical evaluation and intellectual analysis in an area of medical knowledge.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU0436"},"AU4107":{"i":"AU4107","entryRequirements":"A medical degree and current registration as a medical practitioner","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGDipMedSc graduates will demonstrate an advanced understanding of clinical and theoretical issues relevant to a specific area of the health sector and will be critical and reflective practitioners","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU4107"},"OO0624":{"i":"OO0624","entryRequirements":"Admission at least five years after the award of Bachelor of Medicine and Bachelor of Surgery degrees from a New Zealand university.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have demonstrated special excellence in a branch of Medical Science.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0624"},"WK2486":{"i":"WK2486","entryRequirements":"a) Applicants are required to have gained a Bachelor of Sport and Exercise Science at the\n\r\nWaikato Institute of Technology, with a grades average of B or better in the final year of\n\r\nfull-time study (or equivalent in part-time study), and a grade of B or better in the third\n\r\nyear research project (or equivalent); or\n\r\nb) Have an equivalent undergraduate degree.\n\r\n1.2 Selection Criteria\n\r\na) Every applicant will attend a selection interview.\n\r\nb) Where there are more applications than the number of places available, selection will be\n\r\ndetermined on the basis of:\n\r\ni) academic ability as demonstrated in the applicant's undergraduate degree, and\n\r\nii) prior experience in sport and exercise science.\n\r\n1.3 English Language Requirements\n\r\nCandidates who have English as a second language are required to have an International English\n\r\nLanguage Test System (IELTS) score of 6.5, with no individual band score lower than 6.0; or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"This programme is designed to provide education in research methods, academic study and practical applications of sport and exercise science.","graduateProfile":"It is intended that students will develop:\n\r\n*\tThe skills of critical analysis \n\r\n*\tIntellectual independence\n\r\n*\tResearch capabilities\n\r\n*\tA systematic and coherent understanding of the published literature and key principles in the student's specialist area\n\r\n*\tThe ability to undertake effective self-directed study\n\r\n*\tThe ability to apply the theoretical knowledge gained to the effective practice of sport and exercise science in practical and applied situations","educationPathway":"Students may meet pre-requisite requirements for further academic study in sport and exercise science. Students who successfully complete the BSpExSc (Honours) programme to a high level may be eligible to enter a PhD programme within New Zealand or overseas.","developedBy":"Waikato Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Quality Assurance Division, NZQA","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WK2486"},"WI0976":{"i":"WI0976","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand Bachelor of Nursing degree or equivalent.  Applicants must produce evidence of adequate training experience through being a practicing health professional.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will:   * Provide clinical leadership in a range of clinical settings across the continuum of care and the lifespan;    * Generate, critique and utilise nursing knowledge, and contribute to the evidence based of practice through research,   * Practise in joint clinical and academic roles that integrate practice based and theoretical knowledge, and * Provide culturally responsive care and support to people to manage their health and wellbeing.     Graduates of the University of Waikato Nursing postgraduate programmes will provide leadership to the nursing workforce and health services, articulate models of care to address population health needs, produce research that extends the boundaries of nursing knowledge, inform health policy with knowledge derived from critically examined clinical experience and advocate for strategies that address inequities in health care regionally and nationally.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0976"},"VI005A":{"i":"VI005A","entryRequirements":"Entry to the programme will be open to graduates with a bachelor's degree with an average grade of at least B+ in the final year of study.      Applicants may be asked to attend an interview to ensure that they have both the academic and personal qualities to succeed in the programme and practice as registered nurses.  Candidates will be assessed for their ability to make ethical judgements and solve problems. This includes meeting the 'Fitness for registration' criteria in Section 16 of the Health Practitioners Competence Assurance Act 2003.    Students whose undergraduate qualification is from outside health or sciences, may need to complete a formal bridging programme providing basic concepts in chemistry, anatomy and physiology. This will be assessed as part of the application process and selection interview.     Prospective applicants will also need to be of good health and character, these being requirements of the Nursing Council of New Zealand (Te Kaunihera Tapuhi o Aotearoa) for registration. The good character assessment will be undertaken through the interview, identity confirmation, a police vet and referee reports sufficient to establish the prospective student as safe to practice with children, as required by the Children's (Requirements for Safety Checks of Children's Workers) Regulations 2015.     Other requirements for students include that they must:  * be able to travel to clinical placements  * have appropriate immunisation status   * have completed a certified Basic Life Support course.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the Master of Nursing Practice programme will demonstrate the competencies for the registered nurse scope of practice and be eligible to apply for registration with the Nursing Council of New Zealand (Te Kaunihera Tapuhi o Aotearoa). They will be able to work as registered nurses, employed in a diverse range of practice settings across the health care continuum. They will also be eligible to pursue further postgraduate study, undertake advanced nursing practice programmes and apply for enrolment in doctoral research studies.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI005A"},"MY0419":{"i":"MY0419","entryRequirements":"Appropriate degree or equivalent. One year of clinical experience; selection.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be able to critically evaluate literature, research and current trends in speech and language therapy. They will be able to synthesise and integrate theoretical knowledge with clinical experiences, master theoretically sophisticated material, demonstrate intellectual independence, analytic rigour and sound communication of theoretical and clinical material. They will be able to design research plans, form collaborations, engage in rigorous intellectual analysis, plan and execute original research, and contribute to the body of knowledge and clinical practice.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0419"},"OO0511":{"i":"OO0511","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor of Oral Health degree with a minimum average grade of B+ in the final year of study.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this degree programme will have advanced knowledge skills and attributes in the scope of dental therapy and dental hygiene practice. They will be able to demonstrate a high level of research-informed clinical practice, and will have the ability to produce research outputs at a standard suitable for internationally peer-reviewed publications.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0511"},"OT4805":{"i":"OT4805","entryRequirements":"Occupational therapists entering this programme must hold a Bachelor of Occupational Therapy or equivalent.\n\r\nInternational applicants for whom English is a second language are required to have an IELTS overall band score (Academic) of 6.5 with a minimum score of 6.5 in each band. These IELTS scores align with what is required to apply for registration as an occupational therapist in Aotearoa New Zealand. Applicants who do not meet all the academic requirements for entry into the programme can make an application to the Head of School, who will consider the application on a case-by-case basis. Entry to the programme will be at the Head of School's discretion. \n\n\n\r\nSelection Criteria* \n\r\nĀkonga who meet the entry criteria will be offered places in order of acceptance to the programme, until all places are full. They will then be placed on a waiting list and informed if a place becomes available.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The aim of the Postgraduate Diploma in Occupational Therapy Practice is to prepare graduates to be recognised as expert clinicians and leaders in their chosen area of practice. They will have advanced knowledge, and sound professional reasoning skills enabling them to role model, mentor, supervise and/ or lead others within the occupational therapy profession and related fields. Rigorous intellectual analysis and sound professional reasoning will enable graduates to move into new areas of practice where occupational therapy roles are emerging and to advocate for and influence the future direction of occupational therapy practice in Aotearoa New Zealand.","graduateProfile":"By the end of this programme, graduates will be able to:  \n\r\n- Critically evaluate relevant literature and research, across a range of practice areas, theories and/or techniques using the knowledge gained to improve the effectiveness of occupational therapy interventions in Aotearoa New Zealand's bicultural context.  \n\r\n- Analyse and synthesise knowledge to assist others in their teams or the profession to use and apply evidence-informed practice during interventions.  \n\r\n- Demonstrate expertise and/or provide leadership in managing complex practice situations.  \n\r\n- Continually engage in critical inquiry and reflexive reasoning to advance occupational therapy practice in Aotearoa New Zealand's bicultural context.","educationPathway":"Graduates of this postgraduate diploma may apply to pathway into further postgraduate study.","developedBy":"Otago Polytechnic","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OT4805"},"OO0403":{"i":"OO0403","entryRequirements":"Postgraduate diploma in Primary Health Care or equivalent","strategicPurposeStatement":"This degree provides an advanced formal nationally recognised qualification for health professionals engaged in the delivery of primary health care.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0403"},"PR4863":{"i":"PR4863","entryRequirements":"Registered nurse with a current NZ practicing certificate (or equivalent), Bachelor degree (or equivalent); currently employed in a relevant clinical setting Change of Scope stream: Nursing Council approval \n\r\n(International:  IELTS 7.0 in each band)","strategicPurposeStatement":"The purpose of this programme is to provide the health and social sector with graduates who have attained advanced knowledge and scholarship through application of research to their professional practice context.\n\r\nThis programme builds on the existing knowledge and experience of the graduate nurse, while providing an environment that ensures the supported acquisition of knowledge and skills in a specialty area.  There are optional streams in Mental Health and Addiction Nursing, Change of Scope, and Medical Nursing.","graduateProfile":"Graduates will have successfully integrated their undergraduate knowledge and skills into practice within their chosen specialty area.  Graduates will be prepared to apply for progression within the national professional development recognition programme.","educationPathway":"Successful graduates may gain credits towards Master's studies.","developedBy":"New Zealand Institute of Skills and Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Quality Assurance Division, NZQA","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=PR4863"},"OO0221":{"i":"OO0221","entryRequirements":"Postgraduate Diploma in Clinical Pharmacy or equivalent qualification plus registration as a Pharmacist","strategicPurposeStatement":"This degree provides in-depth study, training and supervised research in designated areas of clinical pharmacy. It provides advanced knowledge in the field and the ability to study independently and carry out original research.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0221"},"OO0257":{"i":"OO0257","entryRequirements":"Degree in Medicine and formal vocational training for General Practice and registration for Medical Practice","strategicPurposeStatement":"This certificate provides study at postgraduate level, primarily for General Practitioners.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0257"},"AU5553":{"i":"AU5553","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelors degree with a minimum Grade Point Average (GPA), or its equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"To enable health professionals to achieve mastery of health leadership and management principles.","graduateProfile":"Not applicable","educationPathway":"Not applicable","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5553"},"OO0254":{"i":"OO0254","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor of Pharmacy degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this certificate programme will be able to undertake further advanced-level study or research in the pharmaceutical sciences, clinical pharmacy, or pharmacy practice.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0254"},"AU5578":{"i":"AU5578","entryRequirements":"A relevant Bachelors degree with a specified GPA, or  a relevant Bachelors Honours degree or Postgraduate Diploma with a minimum Grade Point Average (GPA).","strategicPurposeStatement":"MHlthPrac graduates will have developed an advanced set of research-informed knowledge and skills in professional community health development and the ability to apply this to new contexts in health settings. Graduates will be well-prepared for a range of specialist employment opportunities and careers in the broad area of community health development. All four specialist fields of addiction studies, health promotion, Pacific health and population mental health will prepare graduates to work across a wide range of levels that include responding to client needs, leading community development, implementation and evaluating health projects, engaging in health systems analysis, and improving health strategy and health policy development.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5578"},"WK2539":{"i":"WK2539","entryRequirements":"Master of Nursing - Pathway 1 Nurse Practitioner pathway will have the following entry requirements: Registration as a nurse with a current practising certificate and be in good standing with the NCNZ; Completion of a minimum of 3 years' equivalent full time relevant practice within the past 5 years, with at least 1 of the 3 years in full time practice in New Zealand; Meet specific requirements for entry to practice within health services including immunisation, police vetting and indemnity insurance. Entry requirements for the 30-credit Level 9 NURS902 Nurse Practitioner practicum must have: Completed 3 years' full time equivalent practice in the area of practice they are intending to practice in as a nurse practitioner. A working relationship within an interprofessional team and the support of a nurse practitioner or experienced medical practitioner An agreement to undertake the practicum within an organisation that supports nurse prescribing Identified two areas of clinical practice in which to develop the nurse practitioner role, one of which will be the intended area of prescribing practice. One experience must be undertaken with a clinical supervisor who is a nurse practitioner.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Master of Nursing will assist nurses in gaining advanced knowledge and skills to effectively respond to the demands of rapidly changing and increasingly complex health care practice environments. It will enable graduates to participate effectively in the health workforce as highly skilled, culturally responsive, knowledgeable and confident practitioners able to work across professional boundaries to respond to health needs.\n\r\nUnderpinned by the intent of Te Tiriti o Waitangi, the focus of learning in the programme will include working reflexively with clients, whanau and communities within differing interprofessional collaborations and relationships. Graduates will contribute to environments that support and promote Maori worldviews and will proactively identify strategies to reduce health inequities and institutional barriers in a wider socio-ecological context. Graduates will be enabled to engage in transformative learning strategies that build on the strengths, knowledge, skills and relationships acquired through their practice and during the programme. An emphasis on practice scholarship, research and practice-focused learning approaches will enable students to develop more appreciative and critical perspectives about self, others and the context of professional practice.","graduateProfile":"A  graduate of the Master of Nursing will be able to: - Work reflexively in providing culturally responsive specialist or advanced nursing practice consistent with the intent of Te Tiriti o Waitangi and the health needs of specific communities and populations. - Evaluate conceptual and evidence bases for advanced practice and use reflexive strategies to articulate clear reasoning for their practice with clients and colleagues. - Engage in transformational and relational processes that stimulate professional growth, learning and change in specialist or advanced nursing practice roles within interprofessional health teams. In addition, a graduate of Pathway 1 Nurse Practitioner will also be able to: - Demonstrate advanced knowledge of pathophysiology, pharmacology and demonstrate a high level of clinical proficiency in complex client situations and an ability to practice across healthcare contexts. - Demonstrate competence in diagnostic decision-making and planning therapeutic interventions using evidence based, innovative and culturally responsive approaches to improve client health outcomes. - Show accountability and autonomy in practicing within the regulatory and professional frameworks that inform nurse practitioner practice, demonstrating a high level clinical leadership and management. - Demonstrate achievement of NCNZ Competencies for the nurse practitioner scope of practice. In addition, a graduate of Pathway 2 Advanced Nursing Practice will also be able to: - Demonstrate expert and resilient nursing practice within complex and challenging work environments and across interprofessional teams. - Demonstrate effective decision-making with clients and colleagues that reflects collaboration, creativity and leadership in health service settings. In addition, a graduate of Pathway 3 Research Dissertation will also be able to: - Develop relevant, meaningful and cost-effective solutions for nursing leadership, education and practice related challenges in the workplace. - Build resilience and increased capacity to respond to changing population health care needs within service delivery, professional organisations, and communities of practice.","educationPathway":"Possible PhD for graduates following the research pathway.","developedBy":"Waikato Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WK2539"},"OO0504":{"i":"OO0504","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor of Medicine and Bachelor of Surgery degree of a university in New Zealand, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this degree programme will have competencies for professional occupational medicine practice at a registered or board-certified specialist level in any country in the world.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0504"},"AK3806":{"i":"AK3806","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree and relevant professional practice, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PgDipPH graduates will have advanced knowledge in public health. They will have well-developed skills in critical thinking, problem solving, and communication and be prepared for further postgraduate study.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK3806"},"OO0545":{"i":"OO0545","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree in Information Science, Computer Science, Health Sciences, or an acceptable equivalent qualification.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will understand how to critically evaluate and communicate the principles of Digital Health demonstrating enhanced theoretical and technical knowledge of the specialty","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0545"},"VI003R":{"i":"VI003R","entryRequirements":"To be admitted to the programme students need to hold a Masters or Postgraduate Diploma with a minimum GPA of B, have at least five years' professional experience and have established to the satisfaction of the Associate Dean that they are capable of proceeding with the doctorate.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Doctor of Midwifery is designed for established professionals in the health sector who wish to enhance their research-related professional practice and management. Graduates will be able to engage in high quality independent research and inquiry into their own practice and contribute original knowledge to improving health related practice, systems and policy. They will be able to link, in a coherent and rigorous manner, theory and research to questions of professional practice and management of the health system. Graduates will have advanced knowledge of their professional field and be able to evaluate and apply research and scholarly literature. They will adopt an investigative, open-minded, critical and reflective stance in addressing scholarly and professional problems from different perspectives, skillfully communicate research results to both academic and professional communities, and be able to engage in and critique the process of peer review. Graduates will demonstrate leadership in the areas of their professional endeavor as well as high personal ethical standards and behaviours in scholarly and professional contexts, and respect and maintain intellectual integrity.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI003R"},"OO0040":{"i":"OO0040","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Pharmacy degree or equivalent","strategicPurposeStatement":"This degree involves supervised research in a chosen branch of pharmacy. Graduates will have advanced knowledge in the field, the ability to study independently, and to carry out original research to internationally recognised standards.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0040"},"AU0437":{"i":"AU0437","entryRequirements":"Postgraduate Diploma in Health Sciences or equivalent qualification. Candidates for the Nursing specialisation must hold current registration as a nurse in New Zealand.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MHSc graduates will have advanced knowledge, skills and research capability to advance scholarship and research within an area of health science.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU0437"},"CN0932":{"i":"CN0932","entryRequirements":"An approved Bachelor's degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this programme will have the knowledge and skills developed through theoretical courses, scholarly inquiry, and clinical practice experience to go on and complete the remaining requirements to achieve accreditation in New Zealand to work as an accredited Clinical Exercise Physiologist. Once these additional requirements are completed, they will be eligible to apply to the Sport and Exercise New Zealand to become an accredited Clinical Exercise Physiologist.","graduateProfile":"A range of assessments will be used including coursework, examination, portfolio, clinical diary and case studies","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0932"},"AU5779":{"i":"AU5779","entryRequirements":"A relevant Bachelors degree, and a minimum Grade Point Average (GPA).","strategicPurposeStatement":"Master of Clinical Exercise Physiology graduates will know and understand the principles to prescribe exercise and health behaviour interventions to improve functional capacity and to promote physical activity in people living with chronic health conditions.","graduateProfile":"Assessment modes include presentations, tests, reports, assignments.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5779"},"AK3484":{"i":"AK3484","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelor's degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PgCertHSc graduates will have advanced knowledge within a specialist field. They will have developed skills in critical thinking, problem solving, and communication and be prepared for further postgraduate study.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK3484"},"AU5163":{"i":"AU5163","entryRequirements":"Completed a Bachelor degree or equivalent and currently engaged in clinical teaching or curriculum development in a health related discipline for entry to the 240 point MClinEd. Completed the Postgraduate Diploma in Clinical Education or equivalent and currently engaged in clinical teaching or curriculum development in a health related discipline for entry to the 120 point MClinEd.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MClinEd graduates will demonstrate an advanced understanding of the principles and practice of clinical education. They will be able to apply their knowledge, reflect on practice and draw on current research to inform their practice as educators of health professionals.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5163"},"OO0519":{"i":"OO0519","entryRequirements":"A Postgraduate Diploma in Medical Imaging or an acceptable equivalent qualification, present evidence of ability for advanced level academic study, and have undertaken Level 8 research methods course/s to the value of 30 credits and achieved B+ or better.\tThe programme of study shall consist of the preparation and submission of a thesis (120 credits) embodying the results of supervised research on an approved topic in medical imaging.\t1","strategicPurposeStatement":"A graduate who has completed the MMI degree will demonstrate mastery of specialist knowledge and theory and have a well-developed ability in the planning, execution and completion of a piece of original research.","graduateProfile":"NA","educationPathway":"NA","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0519"},"OO0478":{"i":"OO0478","entryRequirements":"The degrees of Bachelor of Medicine and Bachelor of Surgery, or equivalent; applicants should normally be registered for medical practice in New Zealand.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Recipients of the diploma will be medical professionals with a sound working knowledge of the role of CPU (including its limitations). They will have the technical skills to obtain quality ultrasound images, undertake ultrasound-guided procedures, interpret images and safely use the information obtained in their clinical decision-making processes, and communicate their findings to colleagues and patients.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0478"},"OO0359":{"i":"OO0359","entryRequirements":"Registration with the New Zealand Physiotherapy Board; an Annual Practising Certificate; and the equivalent of at least two years' post-qualification clinical experience in physiotherapy.","strategicPurposeStatement":"This certificate programme involves advanced study and practical training in designated areas of physiotherapy. Recipients of the certificate can proceed to further postgraduate study.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0359"},"OO0437":{"i":"OO0437","entryRequirements":"A bachelors degree and eligibility for registration as a medical practitioner and evidence of relevant training and experience","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Certificate is a primary qualification for accrediting medical professionals who work in general occupational medicine. Those completing the Certificate will have attained adequate scientific training and acquired sufficient skills to work safety as the medical adviser to a range of industries. The Certificate course covers a broad curriculum of topics related to occupational medicine based on fundamental scientific principles such as epidemiology, toxicology, industrial hygiene, hazard assessment and control and risk management.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0437"},"MY0736":{"i":"MY0736","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelor's degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Holders will have advanced knowledge and skills in Public Health.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0736"},"AK3805":{"i":"AK3805","entryRequirements":"Bachelor's degree with B grade average OR professional qualification and Postgraduate Diploma in Public Health with minimum B, or equivalent, AND relevant professional practice or experience of at least one year. IELTS 6.5 overall with no band less than","strategicPurposeStatement":"Provide a public health practice and research workforce with community health development skills and perspectives.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK3805"},"AU5067":{"i":"AU5067","entryRequirements":"A relevant degree, or an approved health professional qualification and at least two years of relevant work experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGCertPH graduates will have an understanding of factors that influence the health of the community and provision of health services.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5067"},"OO0426":{"i":"OO0426","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand bachelors degree or diploma or appropriate professional qualification.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Students awarded the certificate will be able to: identify and understand public health issues; analyse and use health data related to the area of Public Health; plan and evaluate public health interventions; and work collaboratively with professionals and the community.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0426"},"VI003N":{"i":"VI003N","entryRequirements":"Direct entry to the Master of Health requires a Bachelor of Health or a Bachelor's degree in a relevant discipline with an average grade of B or better.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will demonstrate advanced knowledge in one of seven health subject areas: health leadership and management; health policy, planning and service delivery; health promotion; midwifery; nursing; professional practice; workplace health and safety. They will be able to apply critical thinking to achieve new insights in their field of health, apply and communication research knowledge in their field and take a leadership role in that field.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI003N"},"AU5742":{"i":"AU5742","entryRequirements":"Completed the requirements for a Bachelors degree in a relevant subject with a minimum GPA.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGCertStrokeCare graduates will know, understand, and be able to apply the principles and practices that constitute evidence-based stroke care at every stage of the patient journey. They will be prepared to work as culturally safe, reflective practitioners, able to function within an interprofessional team.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5742"},"AU5724":{"i":"AU5724","strategicPurposeStatement":"MPhysioPrac graduates will be eligible to apply to the Physiotherapy Board of New Zealand for registration. They will be clinically competent, knowledgeable and informed practitioners work-ready for employment as a registered Physiotherapist within all areas of the health care sector. They will demonstrate a flexible, analytical and research informed approach to advanced physiotherapy practice in health care that will support the development of their leadership skills. Graduates will demonstrate the ability to participate in clinically based research and pursue further postgraduate studies.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5724"},"OO0499":{"i":"OO0499","entryRequirements":"An average grade of at least B+ after completing the first semester of the third year BPharm course.","strategicPurposeStatement":"A graduate with a Bachelor of Pharmacy with Honours degree will be able to: * Engage in self-directed learning and advanced study. * Demonstrate intellectual independence, analytical vigour, and the ability to understand and evaluate new knowledge and ideas. * Demonstrate the ability to identify topics for original research, plan and conduct research, analyse results and communicate the findings to the satisfaction of subject experts. * This is in addition to the expected outcome for the Bachelor of Pharmacy graduate. The Bachelor of Pharmacy, plus one years practical work, can lead to registration as a pharmacist. Pharmacy includes development, manufacturing and dispensing of medicines, and providing medicines management services.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0499"},"AU5544":{"i":"AU5544","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelors degree; or relevant bachelors (honours) degree; or relevant postgraduate diploma; or an approved equivalent qualification; and a minimum Grade Point Average (GPA).","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have the core competencies required to provide effective leadership in one of the specialisations in Health Management, Clinical Quality & Safety and International Health.","graduateProfile":"Not applicable","educationPathway":"Not applicable","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5544"},"OO0155":{"i":"OO0155","entryRequirements":"Medical qualification plus relevant experience","strategicPurposeStatement":"This diploma provides advanced study plus an introduction to research in this discipline which deals with patients who have musculoskeletal and neural dysfunction of both an acute and chronic nature.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0155"},"OO0553":{"i":"OO0553","entryRequirements":"Following preliminary selection based on grades and interview, undergraduates achieving a B+ overall average or above after completion of semester 1 of Year 3 (weighting applied) will be eligible to apply","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this programme will bring cross-disciplinary practical skills to research laboratories, contributing to both basic science and translational research in the field of diagnostic testing.","graduateProfile":"Internal assessment, examinations, research project","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0553"},"AU5522":{"i":"AU5522","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Pharmacy or an equivalent pharmacy qualification and registration as a pharmacist in New Zealand or in the country of domicile.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Pharmacists who complete the PGCertClinPharm will be able to develop pharmaceutical care plans for individual patients in selected therapeutic areas, and to consider issues associated with the implementation of such plans.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5522"},"AU5784":{"i":"AU5784","entryRequirements":"Completed a Bachelor of Medicine and Bachelor of Surgery or an approved equivalent medical qualification and have the research experience, ability, and disciplinary training to undertake doctoral level research.","strategicPurposeStatement":"A DMedSci graduate will demonstrate advanced skills in the definition, management and communication of original research in a specialist area and a high level of potential for independence, creativity, innovation and leadership throughout their career.","graduateProfile":"Doctoral thesis and examination","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5784"},"CN0995":{"i":"CN0995","entryRequirements":"An approved Bachelor's degree,","strategicPurposeStatement":"Students will have developed their knowledge and skills in the area of sport science to postgraduate level and will reflect each of the graduate attributes. They will be able to work with increased knowledge in an applied context. They will be able to seek employment in an Aotearoa New Zealand context with further bicultural confidence and competence.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0995"},"AK3940":{"i":"AK3940","entryRequirements":"Master of Health Science in Psychology, inc PSYC805 and research methods, or equivalent","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the PgDipRehabPsych will have the necessary knowledge and skills to work effectively as Rehabilitation Psychologists and to become eligible to apply for registration under the Generic Scope of Practice with the New Zealand Psychologists Board.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK3940"},"AU5520":{"i":"AU5520","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor of Pharmacy or Postgraduate Diploma in Clinical Pharmacy and hold current registration as a pharmacist in New Zealand or in the country of domicile.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Pharmacists who complete the MClinPharm will be able to carry out research in the context of their practice setting and to contribute to the advancement of knowledge in pharmacy and to evaluate developments in the practice of pharmacy.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5520"},"OO0489":{"i":"OO0489","entryRequirements":"To be considered for admission, applicants must achieve a grade point average of at least A- across all papers prescribed for the fourth year of the Bachelor of Dental Surgery degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this degree programme will have the knowledge, skills and attributes required for registration as a dentist in New Zealand. Graduates will be able to demonstrate a high level of research-informed clinical practice, produce research outputs at a standard suitable for internationally peer-reviewed publications, and embark on postgraduate study at the doctoral level.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0489"},"CN0934":{"i":"CN0934","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor's degree of relevance to the health sciences or an appropriate equivalent health or allied professional qualification.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have gained additional knowledge and understanding to provide a holisitic approach to the assessment, planning, implementation and evaluation of the needs of the patient, family and whanau living with a life limiting condition.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0934"},"AU4093":{"i":"AU4093","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGCertHSc graduates will demonstrate an advanced level of understanding of primary health care initiatives and issues and will be competent and reflective practitioners","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU4093"},"OO0050":{"i":"OO0050","entryRequirements":"A medical degree plus medical experience","strategicPurposeStatement":"This diploma is designed to develop the skills relevant for family planning trainees, midwives, general practitioners, or continuing medical education registrants.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0050"},"OO0256":{"i":"OO0256","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree in medicine, physiotherapy, physical education or human nutrition, or equivalent; plus relevant work experience","strategicPurposeStatement":"This diploma programme provides academic and clinical training in the multidisciplinary area of sport and exercise medicine.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0256"},"CN0244":{"i":"CN0244","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelor's degree or appropriate 3-year professional qualification; or completion of preparatory work prescribed by the university.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates in the health and related sectors who are involved in services or programmes impacting on the health status of the community, families and individuals will extend knowledge and skills relevant to specialised positions in industry, local government, community agencies, and a range of government ministries and services.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0244"},"WK2454":{"i":"WK2454","entryRequirements":"Candidates for the Postgraduate Diploma in Nursing are required to have an undergraduate Nursing degree or a qualification approved as equivalent by the Postgraduate Programme Committee. Candidates who do not have a relevant undergraduate degree or equivalent qualification may submit a portfolio and, if the application is successful, may be admitted on an equivalent basis. All candidates (including international) must also: - hold a current New Zealand practising certificate as a Registered Nurse; and - have completed a minimum of six months of post-registration clinical experience within the previous five years; and - be employed a minimum of 16 hours per week. Candidates for the optional endorsement in Maori Mental Health must also: - have at least two years of clinical experience in the mental health field, gained within the past five years; and - identify as Maori, demonstrating knowledge of their whanau, hapu, and iwi; and - demonstrate an understanding of the role of tikanga Maori within their own nursing practice. Candidates for the Registered Nurse Prescribing pathway must also: - hold a current practising certificate and must have completed three years equivalent full-time practice in an area of common and long-term conditions nursing; and - have a collaborative working relationship with a multidisciplinary team and have the support of a designated authorised prescriber (DAP) as a mentor who will support her/him to prescribe; and - undertake the practicum in an organisation that supports nurse prescribing through policy, audit, peer review, and accessibility of continuing education; and - have identified and have access to an area of clinical practice in which to develop their prescribing skills and have up-to-date clinical knowledge relevant to their intended area of prescribing practice. Candidates who have English as a second language are required to have an academic International English Language Test System (IELTS) score of 7.0 across all bands, or equivalent. The language assessment must be less than two years old at the time of application. IELTS scores used must be taken from a single IELTS Test Report Form (i.e. combining scored from more than one test is not permissible).","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Diploma in Nursing with optional endorsements in Maori Mental Health and Registered Nurse Prescribing aims to prepare nurses as skilled practitioners who are responsive to health service demands for increasingly complex population health needs. It will foster the development of nursing practice at an advanced level within the registered nurse scope of practice, using a generalist and/or specialist focus.    \n\n\n\r\nThe Postgraduate Diploma in Nursing will enable registered nurses to undertake specialty and advanced clinical practice, health education and leadership and management roles.    \n\n\n\r\nGraduates with the Postgraduate Diploma in Nursing (Maori Mental Health) endorsement will provide and/or co-ordinate nursing care to Tangata Whai Ora and whanau in the areas of health promotion, health maintenance and health restoration in both the community and institutional settings.   \n\n\n\r\nGraduates of the Postgraduate Diploma in Nursing (Registered Nurse Prescribing) endorsement will be eligible to apply to the Nursing Council of New Zealand for an expanded scope of practice as a designated prescriber for populations with common and long-term conditions.","graduateProfile":"A graduate of the Postgraduate Diploma in Nursing will:   \n\r\n- Articulate an area of practice in relation to the health needs of specific communities and populations cognisant of the professional, legal and ethical responsibilities for advanced and extended practice roles.   \n\r\n- Integrate advanced concepts of pathophysiology and pharmacology in diagnostic reasoning and clinical judgement to provide skilled evidenced based nursing responses for people with complex health needs.   \n\r\n- Synthesise clinical, experiential, and cultural knowledge to engage in transformational and relational practice with clients that fosters growth, learning and change for health and wellbeing.   \n\r\n- Facilitate collaborative interprofessional team relationships in order to lead innovative and quality health care responses in partnership with colleagues, clients, families, whanau, and communities.    \n\r\n- Critically examine own advanced/extended practice responses to complex, challenging and rapidly changing clinical environments to identify requirements for ongoing professional growth and capability development.     \n\r\n- Actively contribute to the profession through scholarly activities, including research, teaching, leadership and quality improvement.    \n\n\n\r\nA graduate of the Registered Nurse prescribing pathway will also:   \n\r\n- Interpret client health needs to appropriately prescribe interventions and medicines within the registered nurse scope of practice and prescribing authority.       \n\r\n- Determine therapeutic approaches that enhance self-management of common and long-term conditions, in collaboration with clients, families, whanau and the interprofessional health team.   \n\r\n- Monitor and evaluate clients' responses to therapeutic approaches and communicate treatment plans and therapeutic outcomes to other professionals.","educationPathway":"The Postgraduate Diploma in Nursing includes an exit qualification, the Postgraduate Certificate in Nursing.  Graduates who have attained an overall B grade average or above will be eligible to apply for entry to the Master of Nursing programme.","developedBy":"Waikato Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WK2454"},"AU4106":{"i":"AU4106","entryRequirements":"A medical degree plus a Postgraduate Diploma in Medical Science; or a Bachelor of Human Biology (Honounrs) or approved equivalent. B grade average required.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MMedSc graduates will demonstrate an advanced understanding of clinical and theoretical issues relevant to the health sector and will be critical and reflective practitioners","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU4106"},"MY0420":{"i":"MY0420","entryRequirements":"(a) meet the University admission requirements as specified; and  (b) have been awarded or qualified for the Degree of Bachelor of Health Science or equivalent with a major in the intended postgraduate subject with a minimum B grade average across the 300-level majoring papers; or   (c) have been awarded or qualified for Postgraduate Diploma of Health Science with an endorsement in the intended postgraduate subject or equivalent with a minimum B grade average; or  (d) have been awarded or qualified for the Degree of Bachelor of Health Science with Honours with a subject in the intended postgraduate subject or equivalent with a minimum B grade average.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have advanced knowledge in their chosen field, and the ability to study independently and to carry out original research to internationally recognised standards.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0420"},"WK2485":{"i":"WK2485","entryRequirements":"Applicants are required to have a bachelors degree in Sport and Exercise Science conferred by a New Zealand tertiary education institution or an equivalent qualification, industry experience and/or informal transfer of credit approved by the Postgraduate.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have postgraduate knowledge and skills including critical analysis and reflection to enhance career prospects and opportunities in sport, health, fitness & recreation industries.","graduateProfile":"Specialists in sport and exercise science.","educationPathway":"Biomechanics \n\r\nExercise Physiology \n\r\nSport Coaching \n\r\nExercise Rehabilitation \n\r\nSport Nutrition \n\r\nSport and Exercise Psychology \n\r\nClinical Exercise Physiology","developedBy":"Waikato Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WK2485"},"OT4863":{"i":"OT4863","entryRequirements":"Selection will be made on the basis of the following criteria:\n\r\n*\tRegistered midwife, and\n\r\n*\tBachelor's degree or relevant equivalent skills and knowledge acquired through appropriate work or professional experience.\n\r\n*\tAdmission Procedure\n\n\n\r\nApplicants will make an application using the Otago Polytechnic online application process.  Those seeking admission via a portfolio application will need to provide their CV and portfolio with the application form. \n\r\n*\tThe Postgraduate Programme Leader or Head of School will assess the portfolio against the portfolio criteria of the courses or programmes for which the ākonga has applied. Assessment of some aspects of portfolio applications may be through interview.\n\r\n*\tAll documents in support of an application for recognition of prior learning cross credit or portfolio must be verified by a JP or an institutional e-Qual verification service.\n\n\n\r\nInternational student language requirement\n\r\n*\tThe same entry criteria apply to international ākonga.  New Zealand registered kahu pōkai/midwives for whom English is a second language are admitted using the Midwifery Council of New Zealand requirements i.e. to have an IELTS score of 7.0 or Occupational English Test (OET) minimum pass mark of A or B in each section. International midwifery ākonga who are not registered in New Zealand will require an IELTS score of 7.5, with no less than 7.0 in any band, or an OET score of A or B in each section.","strategicPurposeStatement":"To produce graduates who can extend their knowledge and understanding of the theories and procedures that are relevant to the practice environment. Graduates will complete four postgraduate courses, which require them to address their practice from multiple perspectives and to view their midwifery role within the wider context of the health system and multiple social contexts. This qualification prepares learners for further postgraduate study.","graduateProfile":"On completion of the Postgraduate Certificate in Midwifery Practice ākonga will be able to: \n\r\n1) Apply enhanced knowledge and understanding on which to: \n\r\n* assess and manage clinical situations, and  \n\r\n* develop creative and innovative approaches to midwifery practice. \n\r\n2) Apply advanced skills of critique and analysis enabling: \n\r\n* effective problem solving, \n\r\n* development of evidence-based practice guidelines and \n\r\n* safe and effective care which improves outcomes for women/people and their pēpi/babies. \n\r\n3) Apply advanced communication skills and the ability to work in partnership with women/people/whānau. \n\r\n4) Use critical reflection and self-knowledge as tools for continuing critique and enhancement of own clinical practice and role model positive professional and personal development. \n\r\n5) Apply knowledge and skill to:  \n\r\n* guide and support midwifery colleagues, \n\r\n* participate actively in the midwifery profession, and \n\r\nmaintain a midwifery focus within a collaborative and interdisciplinary context.","educationPathway":"Graduates of this qualification will be able to pathway into the Postgraduate Diploma in Midwifery.","developedBy":"Otago Polytechnic","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OT4863"},"MY0341":{"i":"MY0341","entryRequirements":"Postgraduate Diploma in Public Health, or equivalent qualification.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have advanced knowledge and training in Public Health and will be competent independent researchers.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0341"},"OO0244":{"i":"OO0244","entryRequirements":"Postgraduate diploma in Medical Laboratory Science with credit or distinction or equivalent","strategicPurposeStatement":"This degree provides in-depth study, training and supervised research in areas of Medical Laboratory Science. It provides advanced knowledge in the field and the ability to study independently and carry out original research.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0244"},"OO0435":{"i":"OO0435","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Medicine and Bachelor of Surgery obtained in New Zealand, or equivalent. Applicants will be selected on the basis of their ability and experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Holders of this diploma will have undertaken adequate scientific, clinical and operational training to provide them with sufficient competencies to work safely as the medical attendant in a range of aeromedical evacuation roles, or in a medical management role.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0435"},"CN0246":{"i":"CN0246","entryRequirements":"The Postgraduate Diploma in Health Science, or equivalent with a B average; or a relevant bachelor's degree from a New Zealand university, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have extended their knowledge and skills in the health and related sectors, or in services or programmes impacting on the health status of the community, families and individuals. They will have followed an interdisciplinary programme, integrating current knowledge and practice in major areas of the health sciences. They are employed as professionals in the health and related sectors and/or may pursue doctoral study.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0246"},"MY1053":{"i":"MY1053","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Nursing or equivalent plus registration by the Nursing Council of New Zealand.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Holders will be able to integrate advanced concepts and theory with the practice of nursing.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY1053"},"WI0977":{"i":"WI0977","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand Bachelor of Nursing degree or equivalent.  Applicants must produce evidence of adequate training experience through being a practicing health professional.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will:  * Provide clinical leadership in a range of clinical settings across the continuum of care and the lifespan;  * Generate, critique and utilise nursing knowledge, and contribute to the evidence based of practice through research;  * Realise in clinical practice and professional leadership, commitments to Te Tiriti o Waitangi as the founding document for health in Aotearoa-NZ;   * Practise in joint clinical and academic roles that integrate practice based and theoretical knowledge, and  * Provide culturally responsive care and support to people to manage their health and wellbeing.    Graduates of University of Waikato Nursing postgraduate programmes will provide leadership to the nursing workforce and health services, articulate models of care to address population health needs, produce research that extends the boundaries of nursing knowledge, inform health policy with knowledge derived from critically examined clinical experience and advocate for strategies that address inequities in health care regionally and nationally.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0977"},"CN0236":{"i":"CN0236","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Speech and Language Therapy or other degree with relevant undergraduate course work.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates have developed the necessary academic knowledge, research and clinical experience to practice audiology at entry-level. Graduates may work as clinicians in the public or private sector or apply to pursue doctoral study.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0236"},"VI00X8":{"i":"VI00X8","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree in a health-related discipline, registration as a health professional, and work experience in health care.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have advanced knowledge and understanding of complex health care systems, will be able to evaluate health services and critically analyse health policy and practice in their disciplinary field. They will use their specialist knowledge in their chosen health field to improve health outcomes and will be leaders in their health workplace environments. They may hold positions as advanced clinicians, as team leaders, managers, or policy makers. Graduates who have completed a thesis will be able to design and carry out a research study. The Master of Health Care may lead to a PhD.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00X8"},"OO0402":{"i":"OO0402","entryRequirements":"Registration as a medical practitioner in the country where the certificate is taught.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be able to develop scientific, clinical and operational skills to provide them with sufficient air ambulance competencies.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0402"},"MY0725":{"i":"MY0725","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Nursing or equivalent plus registration by the Nursing Council of New Zealand.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Holders will have advanced knowledge and skills relevant to their scope of practice.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0725"},"OO0557":{"i":"OO0557","entryRequirements":"A degree or appropriate alternative qualification.","strategicPurposeStatement":"This certificate is designed to develop the relevant skills for family planning trainees, midwives, general practitioners.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0557"},"CN1246":{"i":"CN1246","entryRequirements":"A recognised undergraduate Nursing degree, a current Registered Nurse practicing certificate from the Nursing Council of New Zealand|Te Kaunihere Tapuhi o Aotearoa; and three years' equivalent full-time practice as a Registered Nurse in the area in which they intend to prescribe.  At least one year of practice must be in New Zealand and have access to an approved clinical placement with mentorship by a Nurse Practitioner or Medical Practitioner.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this programme will have the knowledge and skills developed through theoretical courses, scholarly inquiry, and clinical practice experiences to work autonomously in advanced nursing practice. They will be eligible to apply to the Nursing Council of New Zealand to become a Nurse Practitioner.","graduateProfile":"range of assessments will be used including coursework, examination, OSCE (Objective Structured Clinical Examination), portfolio, clinical diary and case studies.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN1246"},"AK3807":{"i":"AK3807","entryRequirements":"Relevant bachelor's degree or equivalent, minimum B grade average, AND professional practice or experience of at least one year. IELTS 6.5 overall with no band less than 6.0.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Provide a public health practice and research workforce with community health development skills and perspectives.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK3807"},"VI00F8":{"i":"VI00F8","entryRequirements":"Degree and two years practical experience","strategicPurposeStatement":"To provide an academic qualification for midwives","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00F8"},"OO0240":{"i":"OO0240","entryRequirements":"A medical degree and registration as a medical practitioner","strategicPurposeStatement":"This diploma provides study, practical training and an introduction to research in designated areas of general practice. Recipients can proceed to further postgraduate study.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0240"},"AU0438":{"i":"AU0438","entryRequirements":"A professional health qualification or a Bachelor's degree and two years' relevant work experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will understand the factors that influence health and health systems, be able to interpret health data critically and have some experience in public health research.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU0438"},"OO0247":{"i":"OO0247","entryRequirements":"Degree or appropriate Professional qualification","strategicPurposeStatement":"This Diploma provides a variety of health and related professionals with clinically-based academic training in rehabilitation medicine. The emphasis is on acquisition of clinical skills, practical knowledge and an academic approach in rehabilitation.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0247"},"MY0049":{"i":"MY0049","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand university entrance qualification; including specified subjects; or equivalent; selection.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the Bachelor of Speech and Language Therapy with Honours will be lifelong learners and effective communicators, who have the ability to provide evidence-based culturally responsive speech and language therapy services that reflect individuals' goals and contexts. They will engage in collaborative problem-solving with clients, their whanau and a variety of professionals. Graduates will have the ability to critically appraise the literature and collaborate in research.  Graduates will possess the necessary foundations to pursue a Masters degree and a PhD in Speech and Language Therapy.  Graduates will gain skills and experience that will prepare them for a career in Speech and Language Therapy  nationally and internationally.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0049"},"MY0418":{"i":"MY0418","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Veterinary Science degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have advanced skills and knowledge in their particular area of veterinary medicine and will have developed the ability to analyse patient information. They will be specialists in either companion animal health or production animal health and production.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0418"},"CN0986":{"i":"CN0986","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this programme will develop the skills and capacities to provide in-depth health related knowledge in their area of professional practice, be able to use technologies and online communication and evaluation practices to critically reflect on and document their own practices related to the health needs and requirements of individuals, families/ wh?nau and communities where they work. They will have developed the academic proficiency to engage in scholarly work and build expertise in the field and will be able to provide a health service that is culturally appropriate to the individuals/family/whanau/communities they work with. They will be able to critically analyse literature and develop specialist knowledge in their area of interest. They will also be able to demonstrate mastery of sophisticated theoretical subject matter, research, analyse and argue from evidence, demonstrate the qualities of a reflective practitioner and engage in rigorous intellectual analysis, criticism and problem solving within their specialist field of professional practice.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0986"},"CN0933":{"i":"CN0933","entryRequirements":"An approved Bachelor's degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this programme will be able to demonstrate advanced knowledge and skills, developed through theoretical courses, scholarly inquiry, and clinical practice to work autonomously and independently in collaborative allied health teams.  The study and clinical practice hours will contribute towards an application for accreditation as a Clinical Exercise Physiologist with Clinical Exercise Physiology New Zealand, or Sport and Exercise Science New Zealand.","graduateProfile":"A range of assessments will be used including coursework, examination, portfolio, clinical diary and case studies","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0933"},"AU0260":{"i":"AU0260","entryRequirements":"Bachelors degree or approved equivalent qualification and at least two years relevant work experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGDipHSc graduates will have advanced knowledge and skills in health science essential for them to be able to pursue personal professional goals and postgraduate study.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU0260"},"OO0057":{"i":"OO0057","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Dental Surgery degree","strategicPurposeStatement":"This diploma provides advanced study plus an introduction to research in a chosen area. Recipients are capable of self-directed learning and intellectual independence, and can proceed to further postgraduate study.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0057"},"AU5165":{"i":"AU5165","entryRequirements":"Bachelor's degree or overseas equivalent, or a professional qualification with two years relevant work experience in a health related discipline, and currently engaged in clinical teaching or curriculum development.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGCertClinEd graduates will be skilled in applying the principles of adult learning in a clinical setting. They will have knowledge of the evidence base around teaching and learning and will demonstrate a commitment to critical reflection on practice.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5165"},"AU0382":{"i":"AU0382","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Science (Honours) or equivalent including courses in chemistry, physiology or psychology, biology or zoology, physics or acoustics.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have the knowledge and understanding in Audiology necessary to practice as audiologists or pursue further postgraduate study. They will have strong foundations in the anatomy, physiology and pathophysiology of hearing and the procedures for assessing and managing hearing loss.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU0382"},"OO0288":{"i":"OO0288","entryRequirements":"Appropriate Dental qualification","strategicPurposeStatement":"Recipients of this diploma will be eligible for registration by the Dental Technicians Board and will be able to practise Clinical Dental Technology independently.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0288"},"AU5180":{"i":"AU5180","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor of Health Sciences degree from The University of Auckland or an equivalent degree, with an average grade of B or higher in 90 points in courses at Stage III in the Bachelor of Health Sciences or equivalent degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"BHSc (Hons) graduates will be critical and reflective thinkers who have an advanced understanding of the issues of population health and the ability to undertake individual research in this field. With their analysis and research skills they will be equipped for a career in health services or for further postgraduate study, including doctoral study.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5180"},"VI00X9":{"i":"VI00X9","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree in a health-related discipline, registration as a health professional, and work experience in health care.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will demonstrate advanced knowledge in their chosen field of health expertise. They will be able to seek out, critique and apply relevant research in practice and will use their understanding of health care systems to improve health outcomes. Employment pathways may include advanced clinical roles, or positions in health research or policy.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00X9"},"OO0369":{"i":"OO0369","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Students will engage in study, practical training and an introduction to research in aspects of primary health care. Holders will be able to proceed to further postgraduate study.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0369"},"OO0407":{"i":"OO0407","entryRequirements":"Medical degree, registration for medical practice and 2 years of approved experience in general practice","strategicPurposeStatement":"This postgraduate diploma provides a formal nationally recognised qualification for medical practitioners who staff rural hospitals.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0407"},"AU5588":{"i":"AU5588","entryRequirements":"Completion of a number of prescribed courses as part of an undergraduate programme at the University of Auckland, or its equivalent, or have completed an approved degree or postgraduate diploma. Selection criteria apply.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the BMedImag(Hons) will be eligible to seek registration with the MRTB and to be employed to provide medical imaging services with public and private imaging providers in NZ. Graduates will be eligible to apply for admission at Masters level.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5588"},"OO0200":{"i":"OO0200","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree or diploma of a university in New Zealand; or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"This postgraduate diploma is designed to develop public health skills at the postgraduate level.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0200"},"MY1063":{"i":"MY1063","entryRequirements":"Appropriate degree or equivalent. One year of clinical experience; selection.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be able to undertake self-directed study and scholarship, extend knowledge and apply it in clinical practice. They will be able to write professional literature reviews, critically read and appraise research, provide a systematic and coherent account of key principles of a subject area, demonstrate knowledge of cultural and linguistic diversity, and synthesise and integrate theoretical knowledge with clinical experiences.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY1063"},"OO0405":{"i":"OO0405","entryRequirements":"Degree or appropriate alternative qualification","strategicPurposeStatement":"This postgraduate diploma provides an advanced formal nationally recognised qualification for health professionals who practise in the field of Travel and Migrant Medicine.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0405"},"OO0482":{"i":"OO0482","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor of Radiation Therapy degree or equivalent; plus eligibility for registration as a medical radiation technologist.","strategicPurposeStatement":"This degree programme provides in-depth knowledge in radiation therapy, plus an introduction to research. Graduates are able to pursue professional goals and undertake further postgraduate study.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0482"},"WI0975":{"i":"WI0975","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand Bachelor of Nursing degree or equivalent.  Applicants must produce evidence of adequate training experience through being a practicing health professional.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will:  * Provide clinical leadership in a range of clinical settings across the continuum of care and the lifespan;  * Generate, critique and utilise nursing knowledge, and contribute to the evidence based of practice through research;  * Realise in clinical practice and professional leadership, commitments to Te Tiriti o Waitangi as the founding document for health in Aotearoa-NZ;   * Practise in joint clinical and academic roles that integrate practice based and theoretical knowledge, and  * Provide culturally responsive care and support to people to manage their health and wellbeing.    Graduates of University of Waikato Nursing postgraduate programmes will provide leadership to the nursing workforce and health services, articulate models of care to address population health needs, produce research that extends the boundaries of nursing knowledge, inform health policy with knowledge derived from critically examined clinical experience and advocate for strategies that address inequities in health care regionally and nationally.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0975"}};
